rge Herbert Walker Bush (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-01T14:26:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Meacham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meacham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/01058af5-6da2-50b6-903a-10d45fb0b4fc', 'word_count': 1336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01058af5-6da2-50b6-903a-10d45fb0b4fc'}, {'abstract': 'The administration tells older Americans to “check out Medicare Advantage,” but denies favoring the private plans over the original government-run Medicare program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/01/us/politics/trump-medicare-advantage-plans.html', 'snippet': 'The administration tells older Americans to “check out Medicare Advantage,” but denies favoring the private plans over the original government-run Medicare program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Older Americans have been flocking to Medicare’s private plans, which promise predictable costs and extra benefits.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/us/politics/02dc-medicare-print/merlin_147537498_f5f182c8-2b2e-43c9-9f2f-c2bbf45b7e38-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/02/us/politics/02dc-medicare-print/merlin_147537498_f5f182c8-2b2e-43c9-9f2f-c2bbf45b7e38-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/us/politics/02dc-medicare-print/merlin_147537498_f5f182c8-2b2e-43c9-9f2f-c2bbf45b7e38-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'j