39, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6002337c-f7d1-5b40-a413-74b2f62b05c1'}, {'abstract': 'Hundreds of big projects are planned for the rivers that plunge from the roof of the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/01/opinion/himalayas-mountains-dams.html', 'snippet': 'Hundreds of big projects are planned for the rivers that plunge from the roof of the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Along the banks of the Godavari River, near the city of Rajahmundry in the eastern India state of Andhra Pradesh, stands a museum built in the memory of Sir Arthur Thomas Cotton. As commissioner for irrigation there in the 1840s, Cotton brought water to Andhra’s parched lands, turning them into India’s rice bowl.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/02amrith02/merlin_147438855_21ef04da-c42d-4484-9423-ed83ee205dbb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/02amrith02/merlin_147438855_21ef04da-c42d-4484-9423-ed83ee205dbb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/02amrith02/merlin_147438855_21ef04da-c42d-4484-9423-ed83ee205dbb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/02amrith02/merlin_147438855_21ef04da-c42d-4484-9423-ed83ee205dbb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/02amrith02/merlin_147438855_21ef04da-c42d-4484-9423-