icker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Will Now Police the Police?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-01T19:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christian Sheckler and Ken Armstrong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sheckler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Armstrong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/b010fc90-8281-5e1e-9a75-49b834cc33be', 'word_count': 1039, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b010fc90-8281-5e1e-9a75-49b834cc33be'}, {'abstract': 'We are responsible for it. So we must end it. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/01/opinion/sunday/its-on-men-to-end-sexism-in-the-black-church.html', 'snippet': 'We are responsible for it. So we must end it. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was little, my favorite church services were when women took charge. This happened only a few times a year, on the fifth Sunday of a month. But it always meant that the spirit was high and the music was good. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/sunday/02ware/02ware-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/sunday/02ware/02ware-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/sunday/02ware/02ware-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/sunday/02ware/02ware-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1449, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/sunday/02ware/02ware-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/sunday/02ware/02ware-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/sunday/02ware/02ware-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s On Men to End Sexism in the Black Church', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s On Men to End Sexism in the Black Church', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ministers (Protestant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-01T19:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Ware', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ware', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c89d77c1-db02-56d3-8fc1-debe4d774dca', 'word_count': 1052, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c89d77c1-db02-56d3-8fc1-debe4d774dca'}, {'abstract': 'What my student taught me about one of life’s most important relationships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/01/opinion/sunday/an-introverts-guide-to-friendship.html', 'snippet': 'What my student taught me about one of life’s most important relationships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our culture chirps an incessant tune of romantic love — who is marrying, who is breaking up — and we do this on the cover of People magazine, in our most popular songs, even in our unpopular songs. But friendship is fairly unsung. Friendship resists storytelling. A friendship of long duration is not scandalous; it is gentle. Our culture is not gentle now. Friendship endures or it doesn’t. The making of a new friend is not usually marked by a ritual, nor is the end of a friendship. Friendships are mostly mourned in silence.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/02RUHL/02RUHL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/02RUHL/02RUHL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 626}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/02RUHL/02RUHL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 983, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/02RUHL/02RUHL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1398, 'width': 1341, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/02RUHL/02RUHL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/02RUHL/02RUHL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/02RUHL/02RUHL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Introvert’s Guide to Friendship', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Friendship for Introverts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Letters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ritvo, Max (1990-2016)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-01T19:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Ruhl', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruhl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/77279194-f147-55ed-90b4-b20cd6f002a5', 'word_count': 1087, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77279194-f147-55ed-90b4-b20cd6f002a5'}, {'abstract': 'Hypercapitalism squeezes every last drop out of us.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/01/opinion/sunday/the-25-nap-is-worth-it.html', 'snippet': 'Hypercapitalism squeezes every last drop out of us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The season of the nap is upon us. It’s cold. It’s dark. It’s going to be cold and dark for the foreseeable future. Anyone reasonable knows in his or her bones that the proper course of action over any given afternoon for the next several months is to take a nap. And so late stage capitalism has, naturally, found a way to pose the question: What would you pay for one?', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/sunday/02marche/02marche-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 446, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/sunday/02marche/02marche-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 446}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/sunday/02marche/02marche-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/sunday/02marche/02marche-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1522, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/sunday/02marche/02marche-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/02/opinion/sunday/02marche/02marche-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'cap