': 'nyt://article/980bf6c0-6823-5792-b1c1-02b0bacad013', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/980bf6c0-6823-5792-b1c1-02b0bacad013'}, {'abstract': 'Freestyle rice pudding! Fondue-filled squash! Or Alison Roman’s salmon with sesame and herbs! Eat well in the days to come.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/02/dining/what-to-cook-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Freestyle rice pudding! Fondue-filled squash! Or Alison Roman’s salmon with sesame and herbs! Eat well in the days to come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. Our Tejal Rao is in The New York Times Magazine this weekend with a column about cooking freestyle rice porridge— not congee, not jook — with the Los Angeles chef Minh Phan. To accompany her words, Tejal brought us Phan’s delightful recipe for rice porridge with squash and brown butter (above). That’s your dinner for Monday night, though you should make it this afternoon. The day’s rest gives the rice time to settle with the other ingredients and become rich with flavor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Eat-image1-copy/02mag-Eat-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Eat-image1-copy/02mag-Eat-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 452}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Eat-image1-copy/02mag-Eat-image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Eat-image1-copy/02mag-Eat-image1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1541, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank