_id': 'nyt://article/eb1a4645-ec80-5842-aa62-b93a8be365a3', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb1a4645-ec80-5842-aa62-b93a8be365a3'}, {'abstract': 'The death of George Bush has quieted a raucous political system as it honors him for a civility it no longer possesses. But history shows that’s unlikely to last.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/02/us/politics/george-bush-political-civility.html', 'snippet': 'The death of George Bush has quieted a raucous political system as it honors him for a civility it no longer possesses. But history shows that’s unlikely to last.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Just weeks after a bitterly fought election swept Democrats into power in Congress, a Republican president known for reaching across the aisle passed away. Leaders of both parties paid tribute to his civility and bipartisanship, saying the country could use more of that. And then within days of the burial, they went back to their partisan wars.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/03/us/politics/03dc-bush/merlin_147590817_0598ee09-18ee-496d-aabe-d47e5303282b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/03/us/politics/03dc-bush/merlin_147590817_0598ee09-18ee-496d-aabe-d47e5303282b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/03/us/politics/03dc-bush/merlin_147590817_0598ee09-18ee-496d-aabe-d47e5303282b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/03/us/politics/03dc-bush/merlin_147590817_0598ee09-18ee-496d-aabe-d47e5303282b-supe