s', '_id': 'nyt://article/17a67621-536d-53f5-aa88-2c26c4f27723', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17a67621-536d-53f5-aa88-2c26c4f27723'}, {'abstract': 'President Trump does not plan to deliver a eulogy at George Bush’s funeral service Wednesday at Washington National Cathedral.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/03/us/politics/trump-george-bush-capitol.html', 'snippet': 'President Trump does not plan to deliver a eulogy at George Bush’s funeral service Wednesday at Washington National Cathedral.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Former President George Bush made his final journey to the nation’s capital on Monday, his coffin arriving at the Capitol as the rays of the setting sun washed over the plaza where family and friends stood solemnly during a 21-gun salute that began four days of commemoration of his life and death.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bush’s Coffin Arrives at Capitol, Where the Former President Will Lie in State', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bush Makes Final Journey to Capitol Amid Pomp and Compromise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capitol Building (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-03T18:51:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker and Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a49e191-790f-5263-8941-fd72c204e471', 'word_count': 1478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a49e191-790f-5263-8941-fd72c204e471'}, {'abstract': 'Migrants in Tijuana who imagined the United States would throw open its gates at the last moment now know better. Some are trying to breach them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/03/world/americas/migrant-caravans-tijuana.html', 'snippet': 'Migrants in Tijuana who imagined the United States would throw open its gates at the last moment now know better. Some are trying to breach them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TIJUANA, Mexico — The 30 migrants were huddled under a tree on a cold night as an American government helicopter hovered overhead, its searchlight sweeping the tree’s boughs and the hard earth around it. From where they crouched, the men, women and children could see American soil only yards away, on the other side of the tall border fence separating Mexico from the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/04/world/04caravan1-sub/merlin_147697743_d35557f8-5546-450e-abe8-fe0baadabd59-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/04/world/04caravan1-sub/merlin_147697743_d35557f8-5546-450e-abe8-fe0baadabd59-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/04/world/04caravan1-sub/merlin_147697743_d35557f8-5546-450e-abe8-fe0baadabd59-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'lega