Reggie Nadelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reggie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nadelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57e4d719-c008-5923-80b8-7649c05c319c', 'word_count': 1087, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57e4d719-c008-5923-80b8-7649c05c319c'}, {'abstract': 'His Greenwich Village shop, which he opened with a partner in Manhattan in 1967, helped to nurture punk rock and became a haven for fans and musicians alike.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/03/obituaries/robert-plotnik-bleecker-bob-dead.html', 'snippet': 'His Greenwich Village shop, which he opened with a partner in Manhattan in 1967, helped to nurture punk rock and became a haven for fans and musicians alike.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert Plotnik, a lapsed lawyer better known as the namesake of Bleecker Bob’s Records, a Greenwich Village vinyl mecca that survived the dawning of cassettes, CDs and downloading and the death of CBGB, the nearby club where punk rock was cradled, died on Thursday in Manhattan. He was 75.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/04/obituaries/04PLOTNIK1/merlin_147529698_a9dbe62f-af21-4cea-ad2c-25b17896288f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 862, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/04/obituaries/04PLOTNIK1/merlin_147529698_a9dbe62f-af21-4cea-ad2c-25b17896288f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 862}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/04/obituaries/04PLOTNIK1/merlin_147529698_a9dbe62f-af21-4cea-ad2c-25b17896288f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 713, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo