paper/quotation-of-the-day-declaring-strand-bookstore-a-landmark-would-kill-it-says-strand.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Tuesday, December 4, 2018.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The richest man in America, who’s a direct competitor, has just been handed $3 billion in subsidies. I’m not asking for money or a tax rebate. Just leave me alone.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: A Bid to Preserve Strand Bookstore Would Destroy It, Owner Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-12-04T02:18:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/04beaaae-4784-5485-ab9c-0e754b45dcd6', 'word_count': 44, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04beaaae-4784-5485-ab9c-0e754b45dcd6'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Bush expressed no regret for the Horton ad, and some of his longtime allies have long argued that he got a bad rap for something that was not really of his making.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/03/us/politics/bush-willie-horton.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Bush expressed no regret for the Horton ad, and some of his longtime allies have long argued that he got a bad rap for something that was not really of his making.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The tributes to former President George Bush in recent days have focused on his essential decency and civility, and his embrace of others, including even his onetime opponents. But the “last gentleman,” as he has been called, was not always so gentle.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bush Made Willie Horton an Issue in 1988, and the Racial Scars Are Still Fresh', 'kicker': None, 'conte