eight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/06/fashion/06BLEECKER-2/06-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Return of Bleecker Street', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bleecker Street Trends Up, With an Instagram Feel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brookfield Office Properties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bleecker Street (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-04T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karin Nelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5f453cb-d2cd-596b-87a2-3bb2bbd2031c', 'word_count': 1175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5f453cb-d2cd-596b-87a2-3bb2bbd2031c'}, {'abstract': 'Adolescent fixations can be an antidote to the compromises of adulthood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/04/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-rage-against-the-machine.html', 'snippet': 'Adolescent fixations can be an antidote to the compromises of adulthood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you’re 15, or thereabouts, you love the art you love more passionately than you’ll ever love art again. Around that age, your sense of taste has only just recently come into being. Some complicated interaction between macrocultural forces and neurological development has transformed you from a kid with a favorite Ninja Turtle to a young adult with “an aesthetic” — albeit an imperfectly calibrated one, prone to bouts of abandon. Encountered in this condition, Donnie Darko is no mere protagonist; he’s your proxy. “The Bell Jar” doesn’t engross you; it defines you. That Dalí print isn’t MoMA merchandise taped above your bed; it’s a mirror into your soul. This kind of adolescent fervor burns hot and fast and, like any other intoxicant, can lead to a hangover, such that when you later recall an object of youthful infatuation, you may feel compelled to append caveats: “I was going through a phase. ... ”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09mag-LOR/09mag-LOR-articleLarge.png', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09mag-LOR/09mag-LOR-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09mag-LOR/09mag-LOR-jumbo.png', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09mag-LOR/09mag-LOR-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1490, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09mag-LOR/09mag-LOR-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09mag-LOR/09mag-LOR-thumbStandard.