 When you do, wear a hard hat, a harness and boots. Stay safely tied to the tree either by a top rope you’ve looped over sturdy branches above or with two ropes secured around the trunk. To avoid spooking the cat, climb quietly, without breaking dead branches or yelling progress reports to onlookers below.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09map-tip-1/09map-tip-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09map-tip-1/09map-tip-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 633}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09map-tip-1/09map-tip-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 971, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09map-tip-1/09map-tip-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1806, 'width': 1711, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09map-tip-1/09map-tip-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09map-tip-1/09map-tip-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09map-tip-1/09map-tip-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Rescue a Cat From a Tree', 'kicker': 'Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Rescue a Cat From a Tree', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-05T10:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56308fc5-8f2a-529c-8514-a5348d06dbe9', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56308fc5-8f2a-529c-8514-a5348d06dbe9'}, {'abstract': 'Light but still rich, a Middle Eastern breakfast dish is updated for a modern palate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/05/magazine/even-better-than-the-original-ashure.html', 'snippet': 'Light but still rich, a Middle Eastern breakfast dish is updated for a modern palate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sarit Packer is constantly looking over her shoulder, squinting at the past, because more than anything else, her cooking is inspired by what has come before. She and her husband, Itamar Srulovich, steep their employees in the traditions and history that inform the menu at Honey & Co., their warm, tiny, Middle Eastern restaurant in central London. Every few years, they take their cooks on research trips throughout the region. Together they’ve cooked with a Kurdish-Iraqi grandmother, roasted Arabica coffee and cooked biblical dishes with a historian in their native Israel. Reflecting this adherence to tradition, Honey & Co.’s menu often includes a thick, impossibly silky hummus, simmering shakshuka laced with spicy green zhug, a Yemeni hot sauce, and boureka, a classic flaky pastry stuffed with mushrooms and fragrant herbs. Like a flavorful, aromatic beacon, the menu attracts homesick Israelis and other Middle Easterners from across the city.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09mag-eat-image2/09mag-eat-image2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09mag-eat-image2/09mag-eat-image2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09mag-eat-image2/09mag-eat-image2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09mag-eat-image2/09mag-eat-image2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09mag-eat-image2/09mag-eat-image2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09mag-eat-image2/09mag-eat-image2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/magazine/09mag-eat-image2/09mag-eat-image2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Even Better Than the Original Ashure', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Better Than the Original', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbook