, 'url': 'images/2018/11/27/science/27BABIES1/27BABIES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/27/science/27BABIES1/27BABIES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/27/science/27BABIES1/27BABIES1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is It Ethical to Create Genetically Edited Humans?', 'kicker': 'Student Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-12-06T10:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalie Proulx', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Proulx', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82130b8e-bef1-519e-bb18-f3728bddb264', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82130b8e-bef1-519e-bb18-f3728bddb264'}, {'abstract': 'The Navy has spent more than $1 billion trying to develop projectiles to support land attacks by the Marine Corps, with little to show for its investment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/06/magazine/navy-gunfire-ammunition.html', 'snippet': 'The Navy has spent more than $1 billion trying to develop projectiles to support land attacks by the Marine Corps, with little to show for its investment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Navy retired its last aged battleship in 1992, it pledged to the Marine Corps that it would continue fulfilling one of the warships’ missions: naval gunfire support for troops ashore. More than a quarter of a century later, and after more than a billion dollars spent, the service’s intended replacements — rocket-assisted GPS-guided shells — have yet to materialize.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/06/magazine/06atwar-navalgunfire-1/06atwar-navalgunfire-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/06/magazine/06atwar-navalgunfire-1/06atwar-navalgunfire-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/06/magazine/06atwar-navalgunfire-1/06atwar-navalgunfire-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/06/magazine/06atwar-navalgunfire-1/06atwar-navalgunfire-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/06/magazine/06atwar-navalgunfire-1/06atwar-navalgunfire-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/06/magazine/06atwar-navalgunfire-1/06atwar-navalgunfire-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/06/magazine/06atwar-navalgunfire-1/06atwar-navalgunfire-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rocket-Boosted but Going Nowhere Fast: The Navy’s Failed Munitions Programs', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Government Accountability Office', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-06T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Ismay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ismay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b1a1a25-15c8-53ba-ac1d-7e401de5a722', 'word_count': 1316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b1a1a25-15c8-53ba-ac1d-7e401de5a722'}, {'abstract': 'This seaside city offers plenty of Hawaiian charm, and is within striking distance of lovely beaches, volcanic landscapes and a popular local market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/06/travel/what-to-do-in-kailua-kona-hawaii.html', 'snippet': 'This seaside city offers plenty of Hawaiian charm, and is within striking distance of lovely beaches, volcanic landscapes and a popular local market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Travelers flying into Kona International Airport are greeted by a grim panorama: scorched earth and black, volcanic rock stretching from the sea to the mountains. Given all the apocalyptic footage issuing from Hawaii’s Big Island earlier this year, the scene seems to confirm the worst — except that much of this lava hardened hundreds, if not thousands, of years ago. Between the Kilauea volcano blowing its top in spectacular fashion and an August hurricane, there’s no doubt Mother Nature has had Hawaii’s number of late. But the Big Island’s Hawaii Volcanoes National Park is once again open for business. And, on the opposite coast, the seaside city of Kailua-Kona has emerged from the year’s calamities relatively unfazed. Long a favorite of package tourists and budget travelers, Kailua-Kona may not have the lush landscapes of other Hawaiian hot spots. But, beneath a slightly dated exterior, it has plenty to offer. Hawaii’s trademark charms — beaches, wildlife, fresh cuisine, gorgeous sunsets and a volcano or two — are all within striking distance for those equipped with a rental car and a little research.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/travel/16hours-kailua-kona4/merlin_143568996_bd2a8f06-3daa-46c8-a1bf-2b576dca0ceb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/16/travel/16hours-kailua-kona4/merlin_143568996_bd2a8f06-3daa-46c8-a1bf-2b576dca0ceb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/travel/16hours-kailua-kona4/merlin_143568996_bd2a8f06-3daa-46c8-a1bf-2b576dca0ceb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/travel/16hours-kailua-kona4/merlin_143568996_bd2a8f06-3daa-46c8-a1bf-2b576dca0ceb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/travel/16hours-kailua-kona4/16hours-kailua-kona4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 