ny recalled Dec. 15, 1973, as the day “when we were cured en masse by the psychiatrists.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/opinion/06grinker/merlin_147827241_e3762ee2-395b-48ea-a0b5-02e24acd4ad9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/07/opinion/06grinker/merlin_147827241_e3762ee2-395b-48ea-a0b5-02e24acd4ad9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 720}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/opinion/06grinker/merlin_147827241_e3762ee2-395b-48ea-a0b5-02e24acd4ad9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 854, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/opinion/06grinker/merlin_147827241_e3762ee2-395b-48ea-a0b5-02e24acd4ad9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1707, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/opinion/06grinker/06grinker-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/07/opinion/06grinker/06grinker-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/opinion/06grinker/06grinker-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Being Trans Is Not a Mental Disorder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Being Trans Is Not A Mental Disorder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexuals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychiatry and Psychiatrists', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN PSYCHIATRIC ASSN', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-06T16:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Richard Grinker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': 'Richard', 'lastname': 'Grinker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c30d18fb-45b5-5f56-afb7-6b2b7aff255e', 'word_count': 1065, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c30d18fb-45b5-5f56-afb7-6b2b7aff255e'}, {'abstract': 'The pulpy “Bodyguard” got plenty of Globes love and the widely acclaimed “Atlanta” didn’t. Here’s a look at those and other surprising outcomes from this morning’s nominations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/06/arts/television/golden-globes-tv.html', 'snippet': 'The pulpy “Bodyguard” got plenty of Globes love and the widely acclaimed “Atlanta” didn’t. Here’s a look at those and other surprising outcomes from this morning’s nominations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The TV portion of the Golden Globes is equally stupid and special, sometimes nominating people who are very famous but not necessarily doing anything wonderful, and