l', 'snippet': '“Greek,” a cheeky, winking, surprisingly affecting 1988 opera by Mark-Anthony Turnage, is playing at the Brooklyn Academy of Music through Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Greek,” a cheeky, winking, surprisingly affecting 1988 opera by Mark-Anthony Turnage playing at the Brooklyn Academy of Music through Sunday, tells a brutal story. An updating of Sophocles’s “Oedipus Rex,” it’s about — I don’t think this will be a spoiler — a man who accidentally stumbles into killing his father and marrying his mother, sins that cause a plague and are expiated only when he gouges out his eyes and exiles himself.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/arts/07bamopera1/merlin_147755181_159613b8-16c1-4316-9967-3cae1c02e12e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/07/arts/07bamopera1/merlin_147755181_159613b8-16c1-4316-9967-3cae1c02e12e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/arts/07bamopera1/merlin_147755181_159613b8-16c1-4316-9967-3cae1c02e12e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/arts/07bamopera1/merlin_147755181_159613b8-16c1-4316-9967-3cae1c02e12e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/arts/07bamopera1/07bamopera1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/07/arts/07bamopera1/07bamopera1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/arts/07bamopera1/07bamopera1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: An Opera Updates Oedipus, With Peroxide-Blond Hair', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Pick', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oedipus Gets a Peroxide-Blond Makeover', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Greek (Opera)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turnage, Mark-Anthony', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-06T18:09:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/85e65dbf-a0d4-5731-9b4a-afd32edf3929', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85e65dbf-a0d4-5731-9b4a-afd32edf3929'}, {'abstract': 'In Brady Corbet’s new movie, Natalie Portman plays a pop star, a teenage victim of a mass shooting who has grown up to become a 21st-century brand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/06/movies/vox-lux-review.html', 'snippet': 'In Brady Corbet’s new movie, Natalie Portman plays a pop star, a teenage victim of a mass shooting who has grown up to become a 21st-century brand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Vox Lux,” Natalie Portman gives the kind of aggressively big performance that teeters precariously, and at times excitingly, on the edge of vulgar indulgence. She plays Celeste, a drug-snorting, booze-chugging pop star, a banal narcissist who’s having a bad run personally and professionally, partly because she has sacrificed one for the other. Intimacy challenged, Celeste also has serious family problems, and her love life is scandalous fodder for professional gossips. She has a new album, though, and seems on the verge of a career rebirth, one that will affirm her place as a god in a profane world.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/arts/07voxlux-1/merlin_147543450_c37d61d2-d2bb-4a51-aea9-62efa8685608-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/07/arts/07voxlux-1/merlin_147543450_c37d61d2-d2bb-4a51-aea9-62efa8685608-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/arts/07voxlux-1/merlin_147543450_c37d61d2-d2bb-4a51-aea9-62efa8685608-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/arts/07voxlux-1/merlin_147543450_c37d61d2-d2bb-4a51-aea9-62efa8685608-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/arts/07voxlux-1/07voxlux-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/07/arts/07voxlux-1/07voxlux-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 