offman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/829cb04f-3b1d-5428-a11e-514ecda7e87f', 'word_count': 2114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/829cb04f-3b1d-5428-a11e-514ecda7e87f'}, {'abstract': 'Catholic sisters have long prayed for world leaders. This one just happens to do it using a very public platform. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/06/nyregion/dear-potus-the-nun-who-tweets-a-daily-prayer-to-president-trump.html', 'snippet': 'Catholic sisters have long prayed for world leaders. This one just happens to do it using a very public platform. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'When she was a high school student in Maryland, Sister Susan Francois got her first job at Kmart. She then requested shifts on Saturdays and Sundays to avoid church. Born and raised Catholic, she was already experiencing doubts about the role of women in the church and in the institution itself. She spent most of the 1990s as an “ex-Catholic,” she said, living in Portland, Ore., where she went to college and worked as a city elections official.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/nyregion/09nun/merlin_147749760_0fcc177a-7ed1-4ea8-8ec3-612eddfcf9a7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/09/nyregion/09nun/merlin_147749760_0fcc177a-7ed1-4ea8-8ec3-612eddfcf9a7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/nyregion/09nun/merlin_147749760_0fcc177a-7ed1-4ea8-8ec3-612eddfcf9a7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'cap