with the home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/07/business/michelle-obama-women-having-it-all.html', 'snippet': 'Plenty of new research underscores the reality that women are still shouldering, and expected to shoulder, much of the work associated with the home.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Marriage still ain’t equal, y’all. It ain’t equal. I tell women that whole ‘you can have it all’ — mmm, nope. Not at the same time. That’s a lie. It’s not always enough to lean in, because that [expletive] doesn’t work.” — Michelle Obama', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/business/oakImage-1544195346958/oakImage-1544195346958-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/07/business/oakImage-1544195346958/oakImage-1544195346958-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/business/oakImage-1544195346958/oakImage-1544195346958-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/business/oakImage-1544195346958/oakImage-1544195346958-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1080, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/business/oakImage-1544195346958/oakImage-1544195346958-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/07/business/oakImage-1544195346958/oakImage-1544195346958-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/business/oakImage-1544195346958/oakImage-1544195346958-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Does ‘Having It All’ Mean Doing It All?', 'kicker': 'Gender letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Helen Gurley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Having It All: Love, Success, Sex, Money...Even if You're Starting With Nothing (Book)", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-07T15:10:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maya Salam', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Salam', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a29bc612-a0f1-5a92-b950-3b2084f64203', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a29bc612-a0f1-5a92-b950-3b2084f64203'}, {'abstract': 'There’s nothing like the bond between grandparent and grandchild. New books by Tomie dePaola, Cecilia Ruiz and more show it in many forms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/07/books/review/tomie-depaola-quiet.html', 'snippet': 'There’s nothing like the bond between grandparent and grandchild. New books by Tomie dePaola, Cecilia Ruiz and more show it in many forms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Nana never explained to us why she’d chosen to go by a more culturally neutral shorthand for “grandmother” instead of the customary — and irresistible — Greek word “Yiayia.” She was a proud Greek-American who worked as a receptionist until she was 84, listened to Nana Mouskouri records on the hi-fi in her living room, and rolled dolmades so perfectly uniform they belonged in an encyclopedia of domestic miracles. “Chryso mou,” she used to say out loud when she took my sister’s face in her hands, then my older brother’s, and then mine; we were all her “golden one” (“dear one” is the less literal translation), but the fierceness and unselfishness of my Nana’s love made each of us feel as if we’d been singled out.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/books/review/09Anastas-02/09Anastas-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/09/books/review/09Anastas-02/09Anastas-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/books/review/09Anastas-02/09Anastas-02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/books/review/09Anastas-02/09Anastas-02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1314, 'width': 1825, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/books/review/09Anastas-02/09Anastas-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/09/