_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea525fb1-6123-5414-9e40-509bb38d0fd4', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea525fb1-6123-5414-9e40-509bb38d0fd4'}, {'abstract': 'A torn A.C.L. ended Deshaun Watson’s rookie season after seven games. Now he’s back and, with a few tweaks to his game, he has led the Texans to nine straight wins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/07/sports/deshaun-watson-houston-texans.html', 'snippet': 'A torn A.C.L. ended Deshaun Watson’s rookie season after seven games. Now he’s back and, with a few tweaks to his game, he has led the Texans to nine straight wins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — The flashes came, at first, in jagged intervals: a sharp cut, a smooth scramble, an assertive plant-and-throw, the ball whistling toward a receiver. One after another, these flashes tantalized Deshaun Watson’s coaches and teammates on the Houston Texans, and in time they became expectations, and soon thereafter — a few games into this season, give or take — those expectations matured into a state of predictable comfort.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/sports/09texans-web1/09texans-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/09/sports/09texans-web1/09texans-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/sports/09texans-web1/09texans-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/sports/09texans-web1/09texans-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJum