age', 'url': 'images/2018/12/03/opinion/03TP-THEBIGQUESTION1/03TP-THEBIGQUESTION1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Big Question: Have We Left Something Important Behind?', 'kicker': 'Turning Points', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-12-07T20:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SpecialSections', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1aa39955-97e7-58a2-9320-87bfa515a4aa', 'word_count': 3050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1aa39955-97e7-58a2-9320-87bfa515a4aa'}, {'abstract': 'Columbia students didn’t like my joke and they had the right to cut my mic. But we all should have gotten the chance to stick it out. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/07/opinion/columbia-nimesh-patel-comedian-kicked-offstage.html', 'snippet': 'Columbia students didn’t like my joke and they had the right to cut my mic. But we all should have gotten the chance to stick it out. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve experienced a lot of strange things while performing comedy: Rosario Dawson made fun of me while I was bombing in front of hundreds of Bernie Sanders fans. I once had to tell the crowd mid-show that the venue was closing for an impromptu health inspection. On Nov. 30, I performed stand-up as part of an annual event put on by the Asian-American Alliance at Columbia, and about 20 minutes into the show, my microphone was cut off.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/07/opinion/07patel-01/merlin_147854277_a9cebafb-ffde-4f47-8093-d1365e8f4936-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/1