e': {'original': 'By Nimesh Patel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nimesh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb1808dc-141d-5c16-9361-dbd1dc21b174', 'word_count': 1124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb1808dc-141d-5c16-9361-dbd1dc21b174'}, {'abstract': 'The comedian’s brief hosting stint was only the most recent controversy in a year of self-created snafus that included a swiftly dropped new category.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/07/arts/academy-awards-kevin-hart-john-bailey.html', 'snippet': 'The comedian’s brief hosting stint was only the most recent controversy in a year of self-created snafus that included a swiftly dropped new category.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week I noted that the Oscars provide a telling lens through which we can examine the year in pop culture at large. Whether that relevance is expressed through the actual nominations or via the tough conversations about what is canonized and what isn’t, this awards show never fails to provide insight into where we are as a culture.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/08/arts/08oscars1/merlin_147855513_895e59a3-fd05-42b2-926f-a64897cfd570-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/08/arts/08oscars1/merlin_147855513_895e59a3-fd05-42b2-926f-a64897cfd570-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/08/arts/08oscars1/merlin_147855513_895e59a3-fd05-42b2-926f-a64897cfd570-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank'