, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7619106-bdc9-563f-ac27-48266e039ede'}, {'abstract': 'Music’s big awards show is trying to make big changes. So what do these nominations tell us?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/08/arts/music/popcast-grammy-nominations.html', 'snippet': 'Music’s big awards show is trying to make big changes. So what do these nominations tell us?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nominations for the 2019 Grammy Awards have arrived in a kind of crisis mode. In recent years, the show has come under fire for its seeming systematic marginalization of women. And its treatment of hip-hop has led some of the genre’s big stars to effectively boycott the awards, or at minimum, shrug off their relevance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/08/arts/08grammy-noms2/merlin_141668322_834f9279-20f3-469f-b1aa-7641aef27c58-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/08/arts/08grammy-noms2/merlin_141668322_834f9279-20f3-469f-b1aa-7641aef27c58-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/08/arts/08grammy-noms2/merlin_141668322_834f9279-20f3-469f-b1aa-7641aef27c58-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/08/arts/08grammy-noms2/merlin_141668322_834f9279-20f3-469f-b1aa-7641aef27c58-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/08/arts/08grammy-noms2/08grammy-noms2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/08/arts/08grammy-noms2/08grammy-noms2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/08/arts/08grammy-noms2/08grammy-noms2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Grammy Nominations Really Made Us Feel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grammy Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carlile, Brandi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drake (Rapper)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lamar, Kendrick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swift, Taylor', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-08T16:04:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca69ff3a-b479-5055-8248-c5d6a7d3981f', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca69ff3a-b479-5055-8248-c5d6a7d3981f'}, {'abstract': 'A new leader for Germany’s conservatives also brings a new era in German politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/08/opinion/contributors/germany-merkel-annegret-kramp-karrenbauer.html', 'snippet': 'A new leader for Germany’s conservatives also brings a new era in German politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — On Friday Germany’s Christian Democratic Union, meeting in Hamburg, elected Annegret Kramp-Karrenbauer to succeed Angela Merkel as the center-right party’s leader. Given the party’s dominant — if recently weakened — position in German politics, Ms. Kramp-Karrenbauer will also succeed Ms. Merkel as chancellor by 2021 at the latest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/08sauerbrey/merlin_147877767_2de89f74-7361-487e-8e0f-1af963d51426-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/08sauerbrey/merlin_147877767_2de89f74-7361-487e-8e0f-1af963d51426-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/08sauerbrey/merlin_147877767_2de89f74-7361-487e-8e0f-1af963d51426-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/08sauerbrey/merlin_147877767_2de89f74-7361-487e-8e0f-1af963d51426-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/08sauerbrey/08sauerbrey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/08sauerbrey/08sauerbrey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/08sauerbrey/08sauerbrey-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Comes After the Merkel