'headline': {'main': 'How to Foster Empathy in Children', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nurturing Empathy (Starting Young Helps)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Empathy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-10T10:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Live', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane E. Brody', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Brody', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7c9ee71-7dd1-51e8-8f2f-774a0c65a44d', 'word_count': 1101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7c9ee71-7dd1-51e8-8f2f-774a0c65a44d'}, {'abstract': 'Tracy K. Smith, the United States poet laureate, looks at the ways poetry has dealt with the shifting political landscapes of the past two decades.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/10/books/review/political-poetry.html', 'snippet': 'Tracy K. Smith, the United States poet laureate, looks at the ways poetry has dealt with the shifting political landscapes of the past two decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the mid-1990s, when I was a student of creative writing, there prevailed a quiet but firm admonition to avoid composing political poems. It was too dangerous an undertaking, one likely to result in didacticism and slackened craft. No, in American poetry, politics was the domain of the few and the fearless, poets like Adrienne Rich or Denise Levertov, whose outsize conscience justified such risky behavior. Even so, theirs weren’t the voices being discussed in workshops and craft seminars.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/books/review/16Smith-Cover/16Smith-Cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 467, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/16/books/review/16Smith-Cover/16Smith-Cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 467}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/books/review/16Smith-Cover/16Smith-Cover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 798, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/books/review/16Smith-Cover/16Smith-Cover-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1596, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/books/review/16Smith-Cover/16Smith-Cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/16/books/review/16Smith-Cover/16Smith-Cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/books/review/16Smith-Cover/16Smith-Cover-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Political Poetry Is Hot Again. The Poet Laureate Explores Why, and How.', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Politics and Poetry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidart, Frank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'CAConrad (1966- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Curse (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'While Standing in Line for Death (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'SEMIAUTOMATIC (BOOK)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shockley, Evie', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-10T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tracy K. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tracy', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9abb381-8db5-51e4-a379-259851d6e588', 'word_count': 1628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9abb381-8db5-51e4-a379-259851d6e588'}, {'abstract': 'Parents and children have questions, but there is surprisingly little guidance available in the pediatric literature.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/10/well/family/why-is-childrens-masturbation-such-a-secret.html', 'snippet': 'Parents and children have questions, but there is surprisingly little guidance available in the pediatric literature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I first came across the word, naturally, by reading ahead of my grade level; at age 10, I was ostentatiously reading my father’s copy of Margaret Mead’s “Coming of Age in Samoa,” the book that had convinced him to become an anthropologist. I asked my mother, what is masturbation? And I remember her answer: “Touching yourself for sexual pleasure,” she said, neutral and nonjudgmental like the English professor she was.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/well/family/10klassdoor/10klassdoor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/18/well/family/10klassdoor/10klassdoor-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/well/family/10klassdoor/10klassdoor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/well/family/10klassdoor/10klassdoor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 836, 'width': 1254, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/well/family/10klassdoor/10klassdoor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/18/well/family/10klassdoor/10klassdoor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/well/family/10klassdoor/10klassdoor-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Is Children’s Masturbation Such a Secret?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘This Really Is a Normal Thing’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-10T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Family', 'byline': {'original': 'By Perri Klass, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Perri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klass', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4ccebb6-1564-56b6-8097-01a3b4119b95', 'word_count': 1331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4ccebb6-1564-56b6-8097-01a3b4119b95'}, {'abstract': 'Headlines suggest that the epigenetic marks of trauma can be passed from one generation to the next. But the evidence, at least in humans, is circumstantial at best.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/10/health/mind-epigenetics-genes.html', 'snippet': 'Headlines suggest that the epigenetic marks of trauma can be passed from one generation to the next. But the evidence, at least in humans, is circumstantial at best.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In mid-October, researchers in California published a study of Civil War prisoners that came to a remarkable conclusion. Male children of abused war prisoners were about 10 percent more likely to die than their peers were in any given year after middle age, the study reported.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/11/science/11SCI-EPIGENETICS-copy/11SCI-EPIGENETICS-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/11/science/11SCI-EPIGENETICS-copy/11SCI-EPIGENETICS-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 684}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/11/science/11SCI-EPIGENETICS-copy/11SCI-EPIGENETICS-copy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 899, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/11/science/11SCI-EPIGENETICS-copy/11SCI-EPIGENETICS-copy-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1798, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/11/science/11SCI-EPIGENETICS-copy/11SCI-EPIGENETICS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/11/science/11SCI-EPIGENETICS-copy/11SCI-EPIGENETICS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/11/science/11SCI-EPIGENETICS-copy/11SCI-EPIGENETICS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can We Really Inherit Trauma?', 'kicker': 'MIND', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can We Inherit Trauma?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Behavior', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biology and Biochemistry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-10T10:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benedict Carey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benedict', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33c6ee52-ee21-56cb-a5ce-56d98e9881c6', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33c6ee52-ee21-56cb-a5ce-56d98e9881c6'}, {'abstract': 'Women ran and won in record numbers this year, but the ultimate goal, activists say, is to achieve parity with men in Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/10/us/politics/women-candidates-activism.html', 'snippet': 'Women ran and won in record numbers this year, but the ultimate goal, activists say, is to achieve parity with men in Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a month after Election Day, a group of women is still going door to door in and around Atlanta looking for people who do not typically vote. They plan to continue at least until the State Legislature resumes in mid-January, to try to build opposition to restrictive voting laws.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/11/us/politics/11women-politics1-promo/11women-politics1-promo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/11/us/politics/11women-politics1-promo/11women-politics1-promo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/11/us/politics/11women-politics1-promo/11women-politics1-promo-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/11/us/politics/11women-politics1-promo/11women-politics1-promo-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/11/us/politics/11w