, 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/11/nyregion/11subway/11subway-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/11/nyregion/11subway/11subway-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Your Subway Train Might Start Moving Faster', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A 1995 Crash Led to Too-Slow Trains. New Rules May Speed Things Up.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delays (Transportation)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transport Workers Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byford, Andrew', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-10T10:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma G. Fitzsimmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Fitzsimmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/626c74c7-d1a6-508f-9aa2-e0a381574634', 'word_count': 1131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/626c74c7-d1a6-508f-9aa2-e0a381574634'}, {'abstract': 'It took this writer 24 years to get a one-bedroom in the West Village artists’ colony, and now she wouldn’t dream of leaving. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/10/realestate/finding-her-place-at-westbeth.html', 'snippet': 'It took this writer 24 years to get a one-bedroom in the West Village artists’ colony, and now she wouldn’t dream of leaving. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Kate Walter, a memoirist and essayist, was accepted onto Westbeth’s wait list in 1987, she tried to put it out of her mind. “You can’t think about it too much,” Ms. Walter said, explaining that, even back then, when Manhattan still had a relative abundance of inexpensive apartments where artists could live and work, spots at Westbeth, a well-known artists’ housing complex in the West Village, were highly coveted.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/realestate/16renters1/merlin_147713379_1eac1885-f7e7-44fb-8462-cf2de36b7f20-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/16/realestate/16renters1/merlin_147713379_1eac1885-f7e7-44fb-8462-cf2de36b7f20-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/realestate/16renters1/merlin_147713379_1eac1885-f7e7-44fb-8462-cf2de36b7f20-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/realestate/16renters1/merlin_147713379_1eac1885-f7e7-44fb-8462-cf2de36b7f20-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/realestate/16renters1/16hunt1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbna