ump, Donald J', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-10T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Hettena', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hettena', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/01f8c16d-df2d-5b4d-b61a-abb914704690', 'word_count': 1122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01f8c16d-df2d-5b4d-b61a-abb914704690'}, {'abstract': 'It probably has nothing to do with John Kelly’s personality. More likely, the White House wants someone who’s got political skills for the 2020 campaign. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/10/opinion/john-kelly-trump-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'It probably has nothing to do with John Kelly’s personality. More likely, the White House wants someone who’s got political skills for the 2020 campaign. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'True or not, everything under President Trump feels like it has been more bumpy than for any of his predecessors in the modern era. His governing approach combines an unusual faith in his own intuition, a relative lack of interest in policy details and a penchant for demonizing his opponents, real and imagined. The president appears to judge his White House aides less on their governing expertise than on their compatibility with and loyalty to his deeply personal approach to the presidency.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/10dickinson/merlin_147888966_95ea9e26-dd6a-4575-bb91-2ae1cef09d91-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {