 Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ayers, Nick (1982- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, John F (1950- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pence, Mike', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-10T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew J. Dickinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Dickinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/417f735f-3b48-5908-aa80-fccf38276930', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/417f735f-3b48-5908-aa80-fccf38276930'}, {'abstract': 'We spend too much money on college students and not enough on everyone else. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/10/opinion/college-vocational-education-students.html', 'snippet': 'We spend too much money on college students and not enough on everyone else. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Consider two high school seniors — one who exhibits strong academic talent and one who does not. For one, December marks the homestretch of a yearslong effort, intensively supported by his school, to prepare the perfect college application. For the other, December is just another month on the path to, well, whatever might come after graduation. The former will likely proceed steadily toward a bachelor’s degree; the latter is unlikely to finish college if he enrolls at all. To whom does our education system owe what?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/10cassWeb/10cassWeb-articleLarge-v2.jpg'