ople. He fired the office’s previous holder, Jeff Sessions, for failing to provide him personal legal cover in the Russia investigation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/10FREDRICKSON/merlin_147603141_ac4897ee-3d4f-4d1b-8ad5-692db88764dc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/10FREDRICKSON/merlin_147603141_ac4897ee-3d4f-4d1b-8ad5-692db88764dc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/10FREDRICKSON/merlin_147603141_ac4897ee-3d4f-4d1b-8ad5-692db88764dc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/10FREDRICKSON/merlin_147603141_ac4897ee-3d4f-4d1b-8ad5-692db88764dc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/10FREDRICKSON/10FREDRICKSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/10FREDRICKSON/10FREDRICKSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/10FREDRICKSON/10FREDRICKSON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Will William Barr Be Trump’s Roy Cohn?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attorneys General', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barr, William P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-10T15:57:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caroline Fredrickson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caroline', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fredrickson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/06b83c1d-63d5-524c-8b2d-eac93f28331e', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06b83c1d-63d5-524c-8b2d-eac93f28331e'}, {'abstract': 'I have a rational argument for my position. But I want to hear yours. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/10/opinion/im-for-affirmative-action-can-you-change-my-mind.html', 'snippet': 'I have a rational argument for my position. But I want to hear yours. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Affirmative action for minorities in college admissions is once again under serious challenge. For many opponents, the heart of the case against is made by Chief Justice John Roberts’s pithy comment “The way to stop discrimination on the basis of race is to stop discriminating on the basis of race.” The dictum seems to be trivially true — a repetition of the same claim in almost the same words, what logicians call a tautology, like a dog is a dog.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': N