ard to the food aloft. That was when Trans World Airlines opened a futuristic new terminal, designed by the Finnish architect Eero Saarinen at what was then best known as Idlewild and is now Kennedy International Airport.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12TWA3/merlin_147970692_cfcc733b-d24d-42c3-b580-a2930bc56ca1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12TWA3/merlin_147970692_cfcc733b-d24d-42c3-b580-a2930bc56ca1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12TWA3/merlin_147970692_cfcc733b-d24d-42c3-b580-a2930bc56ca1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12TWA3/merlin_147970692_cfcc733b-d24d-42c3-b580-a2930bc56ca1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12TWA3/merlin_147970692_cfcc733b-d24d-42c3-b580-a2930bc56ca1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12TWA3/merlin_147970692_cfcc733b-d24d-42c3-b580-a2930bc56ca1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12TWA3/merlin_147970692_cfcc733b-d24d-42c3-b580-a2930bc56ca1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Historic Terminal at Kennedy Airport Will Have Fine Dining by Vongerichten', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fine Airport Dining, No Travel Plans Required', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy International Airport (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trans World Airlines (TWA)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vongerichten, Jean-Georges', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-10T18:48:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41376107-535e-5871-8bca-554b6c0ddc18', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41376107-535e-5871-8bca-554b6c0ddc18'}, {'abstract': 'The Book Review’s poetry columnist, David Orr, picks 10 collections worth your attention.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/10/books/review/best-poetry.html', 'snippet': 'The Book Review’s poetry columnist, David Orr, picks 10 collections worth your attention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the problems with picking the best poetry books in a given year is that poems — unlike, say, chapters in a novel — are often judged apart from the works in which they appear. For example, “Directive” is one of Robert Frost’s two or three greatest poems, but it was first published in his 1947 collection “Steeple Bush,” which is otherwise generously laden with cornpone. So how good is “Steeple Bush,” then? Can a single astonishing ingredient redeem an otherwise unremarkable dish? By the same token, should a collection that is consistently accomplished (but no more than that) be considered more worthy than an uneven book with a few genuinely arresting pages? When we’re evaluating books of poems, a great deal depends on which noun — books or poems — we think should be stressed.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/books/review/16Orr/16Orr-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 607, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/16/books/review/16Orr/16Orr-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 607}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/books/review/16Orr/16Orr-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1013, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/books/review/16Orr/16Orr-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1212, 'width': 1198, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/books/review/16Orr/16Orr-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/16/books/review/16Orr/16Orr-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/books/review/16Orr/16Orr-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best Poetry of 2018', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Best Poetry of 2018', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Two Thousand Eighteen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-10T19:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Orr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Orr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc539603-72ac-5a8d-aa45-da9a7f555106', 'word_count': 1386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc539603-72ac-5a8d-aa45-da9a7f555106'}, {'abstract': 'Three conservatives said the court was wrong to duck cases with “some tenuous connection to a politically fraught issue.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/10/us/politics/planned-parenthood-supreme-court.html', 'snippet': 'Three conservatives said the court was wrong to duck cases with “some tenuous connection to a politically fraught issue.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Supreme Court on Monday refused to hear two cases arising from efforts by states to bar Planned Parenthood clinics from the Medicaid program, drawing a rebuke from the court’s three most conservative justices and opening a window onto the court’s internal dynamics.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/11/us/politics/11dc-scotus/merlin_138348213_f9abd650-5e5d-4a67-83f2-146a4092f72c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/11/us/politics/11dc-scotus/merlin_138348213_f9abd650-5e5d-4a67-83f2-146a4092f72c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/11/us/politics/11dc-scotus/merlin_138348213_f9abd650-5e5d-4a67-83f2-146a4092f72c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/11/us/politics/11dc-scotus/merlin_138348213_f9abd650-5e5d-4a67-83f2-146a4092f72c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1354, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/11/us/politics/11dc-scotus/11dc-scotus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/11/us/politics/11dc-scotus/11dc-scotus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/11/us/politics/11dc-scotus/11dc-scotus-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Won’t Hear Planned Parenthood Cases, and 3 Court Conservatives Aren’t Happy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Won’t Hear Cases On Planned Parenthood; 3 Conservatives Object', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-10T19:05:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2b9c9b7-33c2-5031-8cae-7f5e4a55af45', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2b9c9b7-33c2-5031-8cae-7f5e4a55af45'}, {'abstract': 'A more affordable version of the luxurious treat is grown on a fish farm near Sacramento.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/10/dining/caviar-passmore-ranch-circle-41.html', 'snippet': 'A more affordable version of the luxurious treat is grown on a fish farm near Sacramento.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sweet spot, when it comes to buying caviar, is quality that costs less than $100 an ounce. This season there are several options for sturgeon varieties like transmontanus (white sturgeon) and baerii at that price, and some for less than $50. At those prices, you can forget genuine osetra. Passmore Ranch sells Circle 41 ($49 for 30 grams, about an ounce), which is dark, nicely textured and assertive like sevruga.  Passmore Select ($94) and Ranch Reserve ($129) are both more buttery and lush. The company also sells crunchy, bright orange steelhead (trout) roe ($13) that comes in flavors, including an appealing mirin variety. An ounce is a satisfying portion for one and about enough for two. This is the first year the fish farm, near Sacramento, has sold its caviar retail; previous supplies went only to chefs.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner3/merlin_147823458_f93bd311-5518-47d2-881c-6759c0aed1f4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner3/merlin_147823458_f93bd311-5518-47d2-881c-6759c0aed1f4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner3/merlin_147823458_f93bd311-5518-47d2-881c-6759c0aed1f4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner3/merlin_147823458_f93bd311-5518-47d2-881c-6759c0aed1f4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner3/merlin_147823458_f93bd311-5518-47d2-881c-6759c0aed1f4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner3/merlin_147823458_f93bd311-5518-47d2-881c-6759c0aed1f4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner3/merlin_147823458_f93bd311-5518-47d2-881c-6759c0aed1f4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Californian Caviar for the Holidays', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Indulge: Californian Caviar For the Holidays', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caviar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sturgeon (Fish)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Passmore Ranch Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-10T19:10:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85ecc5eb-ec7a-5097-8e2a-d6875dba65a8', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85ecc5eb-ec7a-5097-8e2a-d6875dba65a8'}, {'abstract': 'Skiklubben, from Tamworth Distilling, celebrates the nation’s oldest ski club, Nansen, in Berlin, N.H.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/10/dining/drinks/skiklubben-aquavit.html', 'snippet': 'Skiklubben, from Tamworth Distilling, celebrates the nation’s oldest ski club, Nansen, in Berlin, N.H.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in 1872, a group of Norwegian immigrants formed the Nansen Ski Club in Berlin, N.H., at Mount Washington. It is still in operation. In 2015 Tamworth Distilling & Mercantile in nearby Tamworth — owned by Steven Grasse, who created the brand Hendrick’s Gin — produced an aquavit for the club as a fund-raiser to help restore its ski jump. Now the distillery has refined the recipe for Skiklubben, the aquavit, and has made it more widely available. Its blend of spirits, including bourbon, delivers scents of spice and citrus. The requisite caraway is in the mix, but it does not dominate the drink’s honeyed richness as it does in many other aquavits.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner1/12burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner1/12burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 706}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner1/12burner1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 871, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner1/12burner1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1742, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner1/12burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner1/12burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner1/12burner1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For the Slopes, a Ski-Themed Aquavit', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Warm: For the Slopes, A Ski-Themed Aquavit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALPINE SKIING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tamworth Distilling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mount Washington (NH)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-10T19:11:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Wine, Beer & Cocktails', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef857af3-153b-5e8e-991f-902d4cf27cd4', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef857af3-153b-5e8e-991f-902d4cf27cd4'}, {'abstract': 'Meska Sweets, based in Englewood, N.J., makes delicate sweets, which go well with tea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/10/dining/meska-sweets-moroccan-cookies.html', 'snippet': 'Meska Sweets, based in Englewood, N.J., makes delicate sweets, which go well with tea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mehdi Menouar, originally from Casablanca, Morocco, is a founder of Meska Sweets, created to share a taste of his homeland. His assorted cookies, classics like cornes de gazelle (gazelle horns or almond crescents), are traditional teatime treats, as are honey-sesame chebakia and a type of Moroccan macaron, though he innovates these with flavors like matcha. All are made in New Jersey; sold online by the piece, in boxes and assortments; and are gluten-free and kosher pareve.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner2/12burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner2/12burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 