ar about Brexit is that there will be more confusion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Knowing she would lose, Theresa May on Monday aborted a vote on her embattled Brexit deal. The humiliation of the moment was underscored by the derisive laughter in Parliament as the prime minister announced the delay, especially when she claimed there was still “broad support for many of the key aspects” of the agreement. But as the March deadline looms for Britain’s exit from the European Union, the question is whether the search for a compromise has been a mission impossible all along.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/10brexit/10brexit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/10brexit/10brexit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 601}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/10brexit/10brexit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1023, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/10brexit/10brexit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1198, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/10brexit/10brexit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/10/opinion/10brexit/10brexit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/10/opi