', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edwards, John', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-11T01:48:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76b41a22-c222-5c18-bf13-e77ec5836b14', 'word_count': 1416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76b41a22-c222-5c18-bf13-e77ec5836b14'}, {'abstract': 'Nigel Slater’s newest tome is a guidebook to the winter season, with recipes for mincemeat and flavored spirits, and history and lore.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/10/dining/christmas-chronicles-book-nigel-slater.html', 'snippet': 'Nigel Slater’s newest tome is a guidebook to the winter season, with recipes for mincemeat and flavored spirits, and history and lore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This dense, definitive guide to winter and Christmas, specifically an English Christmas, is crammed with personal recollections, history and lore, and threaded with recipes and photos of landscapes freighted with snow. The food writer Nigel Slater says he loves “the crackle of winter” and setting the season’s table by the fire. He tells you how to steep dried fruit in spirits, and he provides recipes for roast goose, fig and blue cheese salad, and mincemeat, which Mr. Slater suggests deliciously sandwiching between slices of toasted panettone to serve with ice cream. The recipes are in metric, but if you don’t have a conversion table, you can wing it for some, like pot-roasted partridge, and sausage with leeks and beans.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner4/merlin_147777876_28388b8c-6a42-4038-8932-a666f53febf1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner4/merlin_147777876_28388b8c-6a42-4038-8932-a666f53febf1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner4/merlin_147777876_28388b8c-6a42-4038-8932-a666f53febf1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner4/merlin_147777876_28388b8c-6a42-4038-8932-a666f53febf1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1343, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner4/12burner4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner4/12burner4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner4/12burner4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The English Christmas Decoded', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Celebrate: The Decoding Of an English Christmas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Christmas Chronicles: Notes, Stories & 100 Essential Recipes for Winter (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slater, Nigel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-11T01:52:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/305ff7f0-908a-52cd-8ec8-377ca7085fa4', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/305ff7f0-908a-52cd-8ec8-377ca7085fa4'}, {'abstract': 'Little Snowie 2, a whirring ice-shaving machine, creates flaky mounds of snow from ice cubes in seconds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/10/dining/shave-ice-machine.html', 'snippet': 'Little Snowie 2, a whirring ice-shaving machine, creates flaky mounds of snow from ice cubes in seconds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shaved ice with a drizzle of bright syrup can take dessert out for a holiday spin. The machine you need to produce it usually requires a block of ice. But Little Snowie 2, with a cute robotic profile, is designed for home use and does the job with ice cubes. Six flavor samples are included. For the season, syrups in holiday flavors, like candy cane, eggnog, fruitcake, cranberry cocktail and pumpkin spice are sold separately. The machine is compact enough to fit in a gift box under the tree.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/12/dining/12burner7/merlin_147853131_57782877