mes.com/2018/12/11/arts/design/atlanta-black-female-artists-art-basel-miami-beach.html', 'snippet': 'Would an appearance at Art Basel Miami Beach help ten women scale the barriers of rejection or aesthetic misunderstanding they found in Georgia?', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — Grace Kisa’s whimsical sculpture, “Love is an Open Door,” features two blue porcelain faces, one with a bluebird on its head, atop brass candlestick bodies. This is her signature — using coils, bottle caps and other unconventional materials inspired by the Kenyan tradition of creating art with found objects. But gallery owners and collectors unfamiliar with the East African aesthetic have closed their doors, she said, calling her sculptures spooky voodoo dolls.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/arts/16artbasel-miami1/16artbasel-miami1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 721, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/16/arts/16artbasel-miami1/16artbasel-miami1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 721}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/arts/16artbasel-miami1/16artbasel-miami1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 853, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/arts/16artbasel-miami1/16artbasel-miami1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1705, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/arts/16artbasel-miami1/16artbasel-miami1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'le