riller, the banter between the sisters Malorie (Sandra Bullock) and Jessica (Sarah Paulson) keeps returning to horses. Jessica, a breeder, chats enthusiastically about her stud as she drops by to visit Malorie, a pregnant recluse who spends her days painting in her studio. During Malorie’s checkup at the hospital, Jessica even imagines how great it would be if she herself existed in equine form.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/14/arts/14birdbox/merlin_147854688_c1076658-2098-442f-a9d5-d001425bfeb7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/14/arts/14birdbox/merlin_147854688_c1076658-2098-442f-a9d5-d001425bfeb7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/14/arts/14birdbox/merlin_147854688_c1076658-2098-442f-a9d5-d001425bfeb7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 511, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/14/arts/14birdbox/merlin_147854688_c1076658-2098-442f-a9d5-d001425bfeb7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1023, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/14/arts/14birdbox/14birdbox-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/14/arts/14birdbox/14birdbox-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/14/arts/14birdbox/14birdbox-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Bird Box’ Review: The End of the World Is Riveting. Sometimes.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The World Ends In Discontent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Bird Box (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bier, Susanne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bullock, Sandra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulson, Sarah', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malkovich, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malerman, Josh', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-13T10:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aisha Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aisha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3e0d377-3650-5684-a40a-c29e6bdc21c5', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3e0d377-3650-5684-a40a-c29e6bdc21c5'}, {'abstract': 'More than two decades after critics declared her “a writer of uncommon talent,” Nunez won the National Book Award.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/13/books/the-friend-sigrid-nunez.html', 'snippet': 'More than two decades after critics declared her “a writer of uncommon talent,” Nunez won the National Book Award.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early in Sigrid Nunez’s novel, “The Friend,” a group of writers gather at a memorial for a well-known novelist who has committed suicide. Most have come not to grieve or pay their respects, but to network and gossip about literary prizes and money and to dissect the latest review of a certain widely detested author.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/14/books/14nunez1/merlin_147633804_1a253536-0e0e-4532-a563-9664f0316324-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/14/books/14nunez1/merlin_147633804_1a253536-0e0e-4532-a563-9664f0316324-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/14/books/14nunez1/merlin_147633804_1a253536-0e0e-4532-a563-9664f0316324-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/14/books/14nunez1/merlin_147633804_1a253536-0e0e-4532-a563-9664f0316324-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1537, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/14/books/14nunez1/14nunez1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/14/books/14nunez1/14nunez1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/14/books/14nunez1/14nunez1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With ‘The Friend,’ Sigrid Nunez Becomes an Overnight Literary Sensation, 23 Years