, 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae95d514-8ffa-5750-91d9-ce26a822fae8'}, {'abstract': 'Amazon is coming to New York despite the city’s transit horrors. Other companies may not be so forgiving.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/13/nyregion/maybe-its-not-taxes-that-scare-off-business-but-failing-subways.html', 'snippet': 'Amazon is coming to New York despite the city’s transit horrors. Other companies may not be so forgiving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The animosity directed at Amazon and the legislators who have opened the velvet rope to the city has been fomenting for weeks, but on Wednesday it reached peak rage. It was then that Amazon executives faced members of the City Council, a body that was locked out of the process of wooing the company here, as well as protesters whose numbers were large enough that the council chamber could not accommodate all of them.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/nyregion/16big-promo/16big-promo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/16/nyregion/16big-promo/16big-promo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/nyregion/16big-promo/16big-promo-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/nyregion/16big-promo/16big-promo-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/nyregion/16big-promo/16big-promo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/16/nyregion/16big-promo/16big-promo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/nyregion/16big-promo/16big-promo-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Maybe It’s Not Taxes That Scare Off Business but Failing Subways', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Job Growth Gets Stuck on the Subway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AllianceBernstein Holding LP', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Partnership for New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-onlyinnewyork', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-13T19:03:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69f714af-cee2-54ef-8a39-3efc54dff0b0', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69f714af-cee2-54ef-8a39-3efc54dff0b0'}, {'abstract': 'In his latest exploration of modern masculinity, the veteran filmmaker plays an unlikely courier for a cartel who finds redemption. It’s a rough ride.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/13/movies/the-mule-review.html', 'snippet': 'In his latest exploration of modern masculinity, the veteran filmmaker plays an unlikely courier for a cartel who finds redemption. It’s a rough ride.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Clint Eastwood has been doing the crusty curmudgeon thing for a while. Sometimes it’s a bad fit, Exhibit A being his chat with an empty chair at the 2012 Republican National Convention. Sometimes, though, he turns growls into meaning, as in “Gran Torino,” about a racist former autoworker who finds redemption the good old-fashioned American-Eastwood way: in violence. That’s a trajectory he’s embraced with varied results, most recently in “The 15:17 to Paris,” a fascinatingly odd experiment in realism that, like many of his movies, is preoccupied with what it means to be a man.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/14/arts/14mule-1/merlin_147855372_36b8ac09-8664-4899-9d42-54d01d50f2cf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/14/arts/14mule-1/merlin_147855372_36b8ac09-8664-4899-9d42-54d01d50f2cf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/14/arts/14mule-1/merlin_147855372_36b8ac09-8664-4899-9d42-54d01d50f2cf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/14/arts/14mule-1/merlin_147855372_36