n private collectors. “That’s a very socialist, democratic way of having to deal with, like, rich people who want them,” added Ms. Cappellazzo. A forthcoming Sotheby’s auction included abstracts by Mr. Richter valued at $20 million to $30 million each.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/15/arts/15REYBURN-1/merlin_148051437_61e7b2d8-eba9-4f59-b056-ce1efcf56b50-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/15/arts/15REYBURN-1/merlin_148051437_61e7b2d8-eba9-4f59-b056-ce1efcf56b50-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/15/arts/15REYBURN-1/merlin_148051437_61e7b2d8-eba9-4f59-b056-ce1efcf56b50-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/15/arts/15REYBURN-1/merlin_148051437_61e7b2d8-eba9-4f59-b056-ce1efcf56b50-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/15/arts/15REYBURN-1/15REYBURN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/15/arts/15REYBURN-1/15REYBURN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/15/arts/15REYBURN-1/15REYBURN-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Painting Isn’t as Elitist as You Might Think', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'KAHN, NATHANIEL', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prodger, Charlotte', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Turner Prize', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koons, Jeff', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-14T11:34:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Reyburn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reyburn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64877f9b-8ce4-511e-aded-790a5e2c78cb', 'word_count': 1242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64877f9b-8ce4-511e-aded-790a5e2c78cb'}, {'abstract': 'A new exhibition by the artist Penny Woolcock shows that, contrary to tourist clichés, England’s famous university city is blighted by poverty and inequality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/14/arts/design/penny-woolcock-oxford.html', 'snippet': 'A new exhibition by the artist Penny Woolcock shows that, contrary to tourist clichés, England’s famous university city is blighted by poverty and inequality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OXFORD, England — It’s an unlikely way for a hip-hop video to begin. At first, the camera shows us a picture-postcard view of Oxford, the famous English university city, from above: spires, towers, trees and lawns, golden in the morning sun. But then the camera wheels round and a beat begins to pul