ound American.” But it’s not true.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sunday is the 125th anniversary of the premiere of Dvorak’s Symphony No. 9 (“From the New World”) at Carnegie Hall. Latching onto its unforgettable melodies, including the famous tune that inspired  “Goin’ Home,” audiences around the world have craved this lush, dramatic work ever since.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/15/arts/15DVORAK-1/14DVORAK3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/15/arts/15DVORAK-1/14DVORAK3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 801}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/15/arts/15DVORAK-1/14DVORAK3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 767, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/15/arts/15DVORAK-1/14DVORAK3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2029, 'width': 1519, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/15/arts/15DVORAK-1/14DVORAK3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/15/arts/15DVORAK-1/14DVORAK3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/15/arts/15DVORAK-1/14DVORAK3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Did Dvorak’s ‘New World’ Symphony Transform American Music?', 'kick