 into a stream to grab a meal. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/14/science/wolves-fish.html', 'snippet': 'Yes, researchers in Minnesota have recorded wolves diving into a stream to grab a meal. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wolves are thought of as red-meat eaters, but a team of biologists in northern Minnesota, near Voyageurs National Park, has documented a pack that often enjoys a meal of fish.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watch This Wolf Go Fishing', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fierce Appetites: Wolves Surprise Researchers By Putting Fish on the Menu', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wolves', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'VOYAGEURS NATIONAL PARK (MINN)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Minnesota', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mammalian Biology (Journal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-14T17:36:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcaddb35-d34b-5b3b-a284-0a61d00672ed', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcaddb35-d34b-5b3b-a284-0a61d00672ed'}, {'abstract': 'Expanding from its Williamsburg location, Nitehawk has taken over the Pavilion in Park Slope, a notoriously decrepit theater that closed in 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/14/movies/nitehawk-park-slope-pavilion.html', 'snippet': 'Expanding from its Williamsburg locati