results from exposed blood vessels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/14/science/albinism-red-eyes.html', 'snippet': 'The pigment shortage may cause eyes to appear pink or red. In fact, the coloring results from exposed blood vessels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A. Eyes are not actually red or pink in animals with albinism. Instead, both the iris and the tissue coating the retina contain very little coloration, and the absence or shortage of pigment in the eye may expose underlying blood vessels.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/science/18QNAALBINO/18QNAALBINO-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/18/science/18QNAALBINO/18QNAALBINO-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 596}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/science/18QNAALBINO/18QNAALBINO-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1017, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/science/18QNAALBINO/18QNAALBINO-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1451, 'width': 1461, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/science/18QNAALBINO/18QNAALBINO-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/18/science/18QNAALBINO/18QNAALBINO-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/science/18QN