el Raymon offers solvers a lovely change of pace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/15/crosswords/variety-cryptic-crossword.html', 'snippet': 'Daniel Raymon offers solvers a lovely change of pace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CRYPTIC CROSSWORD — It’s an odd feeling to love something so much and to be only passingly good at it, but that’s my situation when it comes to cryptic crosswords. It’s also understandable that I am better at cryptic crosswords that are written by American constructors than the ones by British “setters,” because I am less likely to be familiar with elements of British pop culture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Cryptic Crossword', 'kicker': 'Sunday variety column', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-15T17:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6595afd4-6834-5948-8ce2-06a7f6ae80d1', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6595afd4-6834-5948-8ce2-06a7f6ae80d1'}, {'abstract': 'A New York Times investigation showed that data from over a million devices in the New York area exposed people’s daily habits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/15/business/location-tracking-phones.html', 'snippet': 'A New York Times investigation showed that data from over a million devices in the New York area exposed people’s daily habits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The business of location data has grown dramatically in recent years, a New York Times investigation found. Apps on smartphones send precise location data sometimes thousands of times a day. Companies prize the information, which can help advertisers target consumers and investments funds understand trends.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '8 Places Where Smartphones Tracked People’s Movements', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-15T17:02:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Investigative', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rich Harris, Michael H. Keller and Jennifer Valentino-DeVries', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rich', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Valentino-DeVries', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf23a0c5-ed3b-5f63-857b-85e150150cb9', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf23a0c5-ed3b-5f63-857b-85e150150cb9'}, {'abstract': 'At a time when democracies and their basic values are increasingly under attack, the iconic American company has sometimes served clients in ways that directly counter American interests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/15/world/asia/mckinsey-china-russia.html', 'snippet': 'At a time when