n to better handle stress. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a psychiatrist, I’ve long wondered why some people get ill in the face of stress and adversity — either mentally or physically — while others rarely succumb.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16friedman/merlin_148149231_1f4b9724-744a-40ad-ad43-a2600510c027-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16friedman/merlin_148149231_1f4b9724-744a-40ad-ad43-a2600510c027-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16friedman/merlin_148149231_1f4b9724-744a-40ad-ad43-a2600510c027-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16friedman/merlin_148149231_1f4b9724-744a-40ad-ad43-a2600510c027-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1345, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16friedman/16friedman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16friedman/16friedman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16friedman/16friedman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Be More Resilient', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Be More Resilient', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akil, Huda', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-15T19:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea9af77c-8254-59ee-b40b-e35ff7155826', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea9af77c-8254-59ee-b40b-e35ff7155826'}, {'abstract': 'Showing up in person is exhausting, especially compared with live-streaming. But being together is the whole point. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/15/opinion/sunday/church-live-streaming-religion.html', 'snippet': 'Showing up in person is exhausting, especially compared with live-streaming. But being together is the whole point. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I walk into services on Sunday morning, I’m usually about 30 minutes late. Our 6-month-old wakes up from his morning nap at 10, right when the first chords of a hymn begin to be played in our San Francisco church. My husband and I rush to get the baby dressed, fed and in the car. We drop him off at the nursery 20 minutes after all the other kids have settled in, kiss him goodbye, walk upstairs and find our seats just around the time the sermon is beginning.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16TURNER02/merlin_147632778_6dffd07c-9d53-48f3-b187-adaaca0217c5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16TURNER02/merlin_147632778_6dffd07c-9d53-48f3-b187-adaaca0217c5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16TURNER02/merlin_147632778_6dffd07c-9d53-48f3-b187-adaaca0217c5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16TURNER02/merlin_147632778_6dffd07c-9d53-48f3-b187-adaaca0217c5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16TURNER02/16TURNER02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16TURNER02/16TURNER02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16TURNER02/16TURNER02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Internet Church Isn’t Really Church ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Internet Church Isn’t Really Church', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bible', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-15T19:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Turner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2be9a8f-0a07-5c34-bec8-a443e737f347', 'word_count': 1221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2be9a8f-0a07-5c34-bec8-a443e737f347'}, {'abstract': 'Political scientists want to know. They’re not the only ones.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/15/opinion/sunday/trump-authoritarian-voters-political-science.html', 'snippet': 'Political scientists want to know. They’re not the only ones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A recession might be just around the corner, but for experts in the field of “authoritarian studies,” these are boom times. Jonathan Weiler, a political scientist at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, has spent much of his career studying the appeal of authoritarian figures: politicians who preach xenophobia, beat up on the press and place themselves above the law while extolling “law and order” for everyone else. He is one of many scholars who believe that deep-seated psychological traits help explain voters’ attraction to such leaders. “These days,” he told me, “audiences are more receptive to the idea” than they used to be.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16Worthen04/merlin_146273214_97223a1d-cdc9-49e6-bf5a-6fb34d57bea3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16Worthen04/merlin_146273214_97223a1d-cdc9-49e6-bf5a-6fb34d57bea3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16Worthen04/merlin_146273214_97223a1d-cdc9-49e6-bf5a-6fb34d57bea3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16Worthen04/merlin_146273214_97223a1d-cdc9-49e6-bf5a-6fb34d57bea3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16Worthen04/16Worthen04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16Worthen04/16Worthen04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16Worthen04/16Worthen04-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is There Such a Thing as an Authoritarian Voter?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is There Such a Thing as an Authoritarian Voter?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adorno, Theodor W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-15T19:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Molly Worthen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Molly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Worthen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e735650-da9f-57b6-8751-6fdf46046a68', 'word_count': 1774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e735650-da9f-57b6-8751-6fdf46046a68'}, {'abstract': 'Stealth can win out over speed and strength in the arms race of evolution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/15/opinion/sunday/evolution-natural-selection.html', 'snippet': 'Stealth can win out over speed and strength in the arms race of evolution.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The race is not to the swift,” we learn from Ecclesiastes, “nor the battle to the strong.” But as Damon Runyan once wrote, that’s the way to bet. One of my students at the University of Washington, where I taught animal behavior and evolutionary biology, once asked me if the Bible was inconsistent with evolution by natural selection, since — as she understood it — the biological race is indeed won by the swift and battles by the strong. She was surprised by my response.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16barash/merlin_144317826_e6f237e4-2cb6-4576-b27b-c2c2f2cc241f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16barash/merlin_144317826_e6f237e4-2cb6-4576-b27b-c2c2f2cc241f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16barash/merlin_144317826_e6f237e4-2cb6-4576-b27b-c2c2f2cc241f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16barash/merlin_144317826_e6f237e4-2cb6-4576-b27b-c2c2f2cc241f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16barash/16barash-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16barash/16barash-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/16barash/16barash-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Survival of the Sneakiest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Survival Of the  Sneakiest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reproduction (Biological)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evolution (Biology)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Behavior', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bible', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-15T19:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By David P. Barash', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Barash', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/823de8aa-92dc-5028-a5e0-613b8795d779', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/823de8aa-92dc-5028-a5e0-613b8795d779'}, {'abstract': 'The men of this immigrant Jewish community had the synagogue — my grandfather and his friends went every day. The women had the store.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/15/opinion/sunday/family-store-generations.html', 'snippet': 'The men of this immigrant Jewish community had the synagogue — my grandfather and his friends went every day. The women had the store.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was in a daze as I meandered up Columbus Avenue a few weeks ago — politics, the country, the world, you name it — when a pair of pants, a silly dazzling pair of silver-sequined flares that I couldn’t afford and had no cause to wear, called to me from the window. I wondered, as I stared longingly: Why do I, a woman of a certain age, still have a penchant for glitter, decades after I should have outgrown a 7-year-old’s yearnings for sparkly dress-up clothes?', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16schulman/merlin_148149222_2294386e-8c41-48b2-88ac-cb9ac703a308-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16schulman/merlin_148149222_2294386e-8c41-48b2-88ac-cb9ac703a308-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16schulman/merlin_148149222_2294386e-8c41-48b2-88ac-cb9ac703a308-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16schulman/merlin_148149222_2294386e-8c41-48b2-88ac-cb9ac703a308-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1403, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16schulman/16schulman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16schulman/16schulman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16schulman/16schulman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fashion Plates of Schulman’s', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Fashion Plates of Schulman’s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grandparents', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Elizabeth (NJ)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-15T19:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helen Schulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d60ef943-4e86-5548-a57a-34a4b1ab2e74', 'word_count': 1177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d60ef943-4e86-5548-a57a-34a4b1ab2e74'}, {'abstract': 'I could try to find out where my ancestors may have come from, but that is never going to show me what I’ve actually inherited.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/15/opinion/sunday/dna-ancestry-test.html', 'snippet': 'I could try to find out where my ancestors may have come from, but that is never going to show me what I’ve actually inherited.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was growing up, someone was always asking a member of our family, “Where are you from?” Usually, it was my mother. She has high cheekbones, deep, wide-set eyes and light brown skin with prominent freckles. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16greenidge/merlin_148148451_a9fddd53-fb8d-45cb-9bde-6a9ed8d8ac1a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16greenidge/merlin_148148451_a9fddd53-fb8d-45cb-9bde-6a9ed8d8ac1a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 645}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16greenidge/merlin_148148451_a9fddd53-fb8d-45cb-9bde-6a9ed8d8ac1a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 954, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16greenidge/merlin_148148451_a9fddd53-fb8d-45cb-9bde-6a9ed8d8ac1a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1907, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16greenidge/16greenidge-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16greenidge/16greenidge-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/opinion/sunday/16greenidge/16greenidge-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Family History DNA Can’t Reveal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Family History DNA Can’t Reveal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genealogy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-15T19:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kaitlyn Greenidge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kaitlyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenidge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d32451e3-25a1-5f32-ae83-07209a3d9650', 'word_count': 1335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d32451e3-25a1-5f32-ae83-07209a3d9650'}, {'abstract': 'Ukraine took a major step toward establishing an Orthodox Church independent of Moscow, a move likely to increase already heightened tensions', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/15/world/europe/russia-ukraine-orthodox-church.html', 'snippet': 'Ukraine took a major step toward establishing an Orthodox Church independent of Moscow, a move likely to increase already heightened tensions', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Ukraine took a major step on Saturday toward establishing its own, autonomous Orthodox Church, setting the stage for increased tensions with Russia by altering a centuries-old religious tradition under which the Kiev church answered to Moscow.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/world/16russia-ukraine/merlin_148179282_3136044d-3643-47d6-b992-d991ff6e5de9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/16/world/16russia-ukraine/merlin_148179282_3136044d-3643-47d6-b992-d991ff6e5de9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/world/16russia-ukraine/merlin_148179282_3136044d-3643-47d6-b992-d991ff6e5de9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/world/16russia-ukraine/merlin_148179282_3136044d-3643-47d6-b992-d991ff6e5de9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1422, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/world/16russia-ukraine/17ukraine-church-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/16/world/16russia-ukraine/17ukraine-church-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/16/world/16russia-ukraine/17ukraine-church-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Russia Tensions, Ukraine Moves Toward Separate Church', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ukraine Church Moves to Break With Moscow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Orthodox Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Martial Law', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eastern Orthodox Church', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poroshenko, Petro Olekseyevich', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-15T20:16:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7c62df5-2731-5144-b37d-5902d68f50b4', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7c62df5-2731-5144-b37d-5902d68f50b4'}, {'abstract': 'The secretary of the Interior departs under a cascade of ethics investigations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/15/opinion/ryan-zinke-interior-resigns-trump.html', 'snippet': 'The secretary of the Interior departs under a cascade of ethics investigations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ryan Zinke, the secretary of the Interior, is the second devoted cheerleader for President Trump’s boneheaded strategy of “energy dominance” to be ushered out the door. The first was Scott Pruitt, the administrator of the Environmental Protection Agency. Like Mr. Pruitt, Mr. Zinke leaves under a cloud of possible ethical violations. Also like Mr. Pruitt, Mr. Zinke promoted the rapid development of fossil fuels — coal in Mr. Pruitt’s case, oil and gas in Mr. Zinke’s — at a time when nearly every reputable scientist says that the world needs to produce and consume less of these fuels, not more, and swiftly replace them with carbon-free alternatives to avert the worst consequences of climate change. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/opinion/15zinke-edt/merlin_142425153_edfee75c-575a-4e3c-a7f1-657c3359c18c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/18/opinion/15zinke-edt/merlin_142425153_edfee75c-575a-4e3c-a7f1-657c3359c18c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/opinion/15zinke-edt/merlin_142425153_edfee75c-575a-4e3c-a7f1-657c3359c18c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/opinion/15zinke-edt/merlin_142425153_edfee75c-575a-4e3c-a7f1-657c3359c18c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/opinion/15zinke-edt/15zinke-edt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 