nterviews with witnesses, clearly shows the military opening fire on unarmed demonstrators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/17/world/africa/nigeria-military-abuses.html', 'snippet': 'A close review of video from the largest and most deadly of the protests, as well as interviews with witnesses, clearly shows the military opening fire on unarmed demonstrators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABUJA, Nigeria — The message sent on Twitter was clear: When Nigerian soldiers opened fire on rock-throwing protesters in late October, Nigerian officials swiftly defended them, saying their forces had simply done what President Trump told American soldiers to do in the same situation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nigeria Says Soldiers Who Killed Marchers Were Provoked. Video Shows Otherwise.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Video Belies Nigeria’s Claim That Soldiers Were Provoked to Shoot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buhari, Muhammadu', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic Movement (Nigeria)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-17T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dionne Searcey and Emmanuel Akinwotu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dionne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Searcey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'o