Dec. 13 puzzle by John Westwig, and not a minute too soon; it has taken the beverage world by storm as an ingredient in smoothies and baked goods, as a coffee replacement and even in face masks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/17/crosswords/17wordplay-wthit-art-matcha/17wordplay-wthit-art-matcha-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/17/crosswords/17wordplay-wthit-art-matcha/17wordplay-wthit-art-matcha-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/17/crosswords/17wordplay-wthit-art-matcha/17wordplay-wthit-art-matcha-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/17/crosswords/17wordplay-wthit-art-matcha/17wordplay-wthit-art-matcha-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1354, 'width': 2030, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/17/crosswords/17wordplay-wthit-art-matcha/17wordplay-wthit-art-matcha-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/17/crosswords/17wordplay-wthit-art-matcha/17wordplay-wthit-art-matcha-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/17/crosswords/17wordplay-wthit-art-matcha/17wordplay-wthit-art-matcha-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What the Heck Is That?', 'kicker': 'words to know', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-17T15:30:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e0d4e20-596b-5f43-b80f-1b49e3d3a3bb', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e0d4e20-596b-5f43-b80f-1b49e3d3a3bb'}, {'abstract': 'Revel in the magic of a perfect chicken salad recipe, and plan to make vegan Thai curry regardless of your vegan status.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/17/dining/what-to-cook-right-now.html', 'snippet': 'Revel in the magic of a perfect chicken salad recipe, and plan to make vegan Thai curry regardless of your vegan status.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. I once had a job at a posh little deli attached to a restaurant in a charming part of town. I’d arrive before dawn and heat a huge vat of water on the stove, perfume it with peppercorns, then slide five or six chickens into it to poach. I’d make mayonnaise while the chicken simmered, toast pecans, slice celery and grapes. When the chickens were done, cooked to softness, moist and fragrant, I’d allow them to cool, then shred them into a wide, wide bowl. Mixed with my mayonnaise, a whisper of mustard, some lemon juice, a little yogurt, a pillow of tarragon, the nuts and the grapes, it became a salad of uncommon luxury, the filling for sandwiches I’d sell for lunch and the center of cold prepared meals I’d offer for dinner after that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/13/dining/13RECIPE-LAB1-WEB/13RECIPE-LAB1-WEB-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 414, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/07/13/dining/13RECIPE-LAB1-WEB/13RECIPE-LAB1-WEB-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 414}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/13/dining/13RECIPE-LAB1-WEB/13RECIPE-LAB1-WEB-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/13/dining/13RECIPE-LAB1-WEB/13RECIPE-LAB1-WEB-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1220, 'width': 1766, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/13/dining/13RECIPE-LAB1-WEB/13RECIPE-LAB1-WEB-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/07/13/dining/13RECIPE-LAB1-WEB/13RECIPE-LAB1-WEB-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/13/dining/13RECIPE-LAB1-WEB/13RECIPE-LAB1-WEB-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Cook Right Now', 'kicker': 'What to Cook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-17T15:30:01+0000', 'doc