lls of Khalilah EL-Amin’s apartment are adorned with family photos, homemade paintings and inspirational sayings.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/20/neediest-cases/20ncf-elamin1/merlin_147059649_4b2ce4f9-6830-4ef3-b6d5-68cc3fe77c61-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/20/neediest-cases/20ncf-elamin1/merlin_147059649_4b2ce4f9-6830-4ef3-b6d5-68cc3fe77c61-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/20/neediest-cases/20ncf-elamin1/merlin_147059649_4b2ce4f9-6830-4ef3-b6d5-68cc3fe77c61-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/20/neediest-cases/20ncf-elamin1/merlin_147059649_4b2ce4f9-6830-4ef3-b6d5-68cc3fe77c61-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/20/neediest-cases/20ncf-elamin1/00ncf-elamin1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/20/neediest-cases/20ncf-elamin1/00ncf-elamin1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/20/neediest-cases/20ncf-elamin1/00ncf-elamin1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Little Help, a New Job, 2 Books and Big Ideas', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases Fund', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Little Help Brings a New Job and Some Big Ideas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Community Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-18T16:02:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Neediest Cases', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Mele', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mele', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65abff8e-db5a-515d-9d45-a561f40bfce4', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65abff8e-db5a-515d-9d45-a561f40bfce4'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around the newsroom are reading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/18/books/review/new-noteworthy-emily-steel.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around the newsroom are reading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE HEBREW BIBLE Translated by Robert Alter. (Norton, $125.) Alter is the first person to single-handedly produce a translation of the complete Hebrew Bible. His achievement is monumental, marked by literary grace and intelligent commentary. TO OBAMA By Jeanne Marie Laskas. (Random House, $28.) Every evening of his presidency, Barack Obama read 10 letters from the thousands that arrived at the White House daily. These are some of the pleas, rants and sad stories he received. DANCE IN AMERICA Edited by Mindy Aloff, foreword by Robert Gottlieb. (Library of America, $40.) This wide-ranging collection of writing about dance — 100 entries spanning three centuries, including pieces by the likes of Josephine Baker and Susan Sontag — tells the story of an evolving and deeply felt art form. THE NEW YORK TIMES BOOK OF POLITICS Edited by Andrew Rosenthal, foreword by Maureen Dowd. (Sterling, $27.95.) Can you capture in one book the sweep of politics over the past 167 years? Rosenthal gives it a shot in this engaging compendium. REDISCOVERING TRAVEL By Seth Kugel. (Liveright, $26.95.) Kugel, who wrote the Frugal Traveler column for The Times for six years, makes a case for returning to an older form of travel, before Google Maps and TripAdvisor, when curiosity about the unknown was the guiding principle.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/books/23NewNoteworthy/23NewNoteworthy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/23/books/23NewNoteworthy/23NewNoteworthy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/books/23NewNoteworthy/23NewNoteworthy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/books/23NewNoteworthy/23NewNoteworthy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/books/23NewNoteworthy/23NewNoteworthy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/23/books/23NewNoteworthy/2