: None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/autossell/00well_whippman/00well_whippman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/18/autossell/00well_whippman/00well_whippman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/18/autossell/00well_whippman/00well_whippman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Power of the ‘Little Comment’ in Mother-Daughter Relationships', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-20T10:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Family', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth Whippman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Whippman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fed27ba7-c851-5c9b-ad32-6201e26bbc87', 'word_count': 1165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fed27ba7-c851-5c9b-ad32-6201e26bbc87'}, {'abstract': 'I’ve been lucky that most of my care is delivered with tenderness, despite the fact that cancer patients are routinely exposed to brutal procedures. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/20/well/live/in-praise-of-gentleness.html', 'snippet': 'I’ve been lucky that most of my care is delivered with tenderness, despite the fact that cancer patients are routinely exposed to brutal procedures. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Often I have lain under a sheet on a gurney in a hospital hall, dreading what would happen during some ghastly procedure related to my ovarian cancer. One incident, filtered through a narcotic haze, still haunts me, though it must have occurred more than five years ago. I watched the ceiling roll by as someone pushed me down a corridor into a freezing operating room. Under bright lights, I had to be moved from the cart onto a table and repositioned on my stomach.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/13/well/goya-portrait/goya-portrait-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 894, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/13/well/goya-portrait/goya-portrait-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 894}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/13/well/goya-portrait/goya-portrait-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/13/well/goya-portrait/goya-portrait-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1376, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/13/well/goya-portrait/goya-portrait-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/13/well/goya-portrait/goya-portrait-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/13/well/goya-portrait/goya-portrait-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Praise of Gentleness ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Touch (Sense)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-20T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Live', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Gubar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gubar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32266152-c595-5010-bc47-de4b681d9493', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32266152-c595-5010-bc47-de4b681d9493'}, {'abstract': 'You don’t have to lie to children in order to delight them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/20/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-tio-de-nadal.html', 'snippet': 'You don’t have to lie to children in order to delight them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was 5, I stood in my grandparents’ small, pipe-smoke-filled, well-loved apartment in Barcelona on Christmas Day, getting ready to hit a wooden log. The log wore a painted, smiling face and a red hat; its front was propped up on two legs like a sitting dog, and the rest of its body was covered with a checkered blanket. My grandmother had taken it out of storage, as she did every year, and lovingly set it up on the floor, dropping some clementine peels around its base to show that it had been fed. My role, as the youngest child in the family, was to sing to the log while I hit it with a stick, thus prompting it to defecate presents and nougat — for the log was magic, and this is what it did.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/magazine/23mag-LOR/23mag-LOR-articleLarge.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/23/magazine/23mag-LOR/23mag-LOR-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/magazine/23mag-LOR/23mag-LOR-jumbo.png', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/magazine/23mag-LOR/23mag-LOR-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/magazine/23mag-LOR/23mag-LOR-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/23/magazine/23mag-LOR/23mag-LOR-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/magazine/23mag-LOR/23mag-LOR-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: Tió de Nadal', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tió de Nadal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Catalonia (Spain)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-20T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marta Bausells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bausells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33e44198-0cc8-5535-b341-38180e664660', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33e44198-0cc8-5535-b341-38180e664660'}, {'abstract': 'How does this word reflect the social or political issues of 2018?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/20/learning/what-is-your-choice-for-word-of-the-year.html', 'snippet': 'How does this word reflect the social or political issues of 2018?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What one word best represents 2018? Why?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/15/arts/15wordoftheyear/15wordoftheyear-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/15/arts/15wordoftheyear/15wordoftheyear-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/15/arts/15wordoftheyear/15wordoftheyear-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/15/arts/15wordoftheyear/15wordoftheyear-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1251, 'width': 1877, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/15/arts/15wordoftheyear/15wordoftheyear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/15/arts/15wordoftheyear/15wordoftheyear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/15/arts/15wordoftheyear/15wordoftheyear-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Is Your Choice for Word of the Year?', 'kicker': 'Student Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-12-20T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Engle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Engle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/820f3ef4-57f1-5314-a528-21ae012e2200', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/820f3ef4-57f1-5314-a528-21ae012e2200'}, {'abstract': 'From ‘Girlfight’ to ‘Destroyer,’ her movies are distinguished by her willingness not to revel in brutality but to look it in the face.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/20/magazine/destroyer-movie-karyn-kusama.html', 'snippet': 'From ‘Girlfight’ to ‘Destroyer,’ her movies are distinguished by her willingness not to revel in brutality but to look it in the face.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Karyn Kusama was 10, she went with her mother and her younger brother and sister to see an interesting new movie, David Lynch’s “Eraserhead,” at the art house in downtown St. Louis. In Lynch’s surreal black-and-white fantasia, an alien baby — possibly a lamb fetus, though Lynch has never revealed what he used — grows sicker and sicker until its bandages are removed and its organs fall apart. At some point, one of Kusama’s siblings started crying, and her mother asked Kusama to take them both outside so she could finish watching the movie in peace. While her mom — whose taste did not normally run to grotesquerie — sat in the theater laughing as if “Eraserhead” were the comedy of the year and her sibling sobbed in the lobby, Kusama stood on tippy toes, trying to glimpse the screen through the porthole window.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/magazine/23mag-Kusama-slide-272L/23mag-Kusama-slide-272L-articleLarge.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/23/magazine/23mag-Kusama-slide-272L/23mag-Kusama-slide-272L-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/magazine/23mag-Kusama-slide-272L/23mag-Kusama-slide-272L-jumbo.png', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/magazine/23mag-Kusama-slide-272L/23mag-Kusama-slide-272L-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/magazine/23mag-Kusama-slide-272L/23mag-Kusama-slide-272L-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/23/mag