web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/20/movies/welcome-to-marwen-review.html', 'snippet': 'Steve Carell portrays a wounded artist in Robert Zemeckis’s latest trip to the uncanny valley.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Welcome to Marwen” is about a grown man who plays with toys. That’s what it looks like Mark Hogancamp is doing, anyway. His house in Kingston, N.Y., is full of dolls, action figures and accessories arranged into a make-believe Belgian village he has named Marwen. In Mark’s fantasy world — which frequently comes to jarring digital life onscreen — his G.I. Joe-like alter ego, a hard-boiled, hard-plastic American soldier known as Hogie, does battle with Nazis, aided by a revolving cast of women with Barbie-doll physiques.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/21/arts/21marwen/merlin_148187010_c25954a9-80f2-4e84-a9c1-7fbda3c7e3ae-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/21/arts/21marwen/merlin_148187010_c25954a9-80f2-4e84-a9c1-7fbda3c7e3ae-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/21/arts/21marwen/merlin_148187010_c25954a9-80f2-4e84-a9c1-7fbda3c7e3ae-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/21/arts/21marwen/merlin_148187010_c25954a9-80f2-4e84-a9c1-7fbda3c7e3ae-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/21/arts/21marwen/21marwen1-thumbStandard.jpg',