real.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I am a killing machine but a happy one — I get all my resentments out in my books,” Louise Penny told The Times earlier this year. Her latest novel, “Kingdom of the Blind,” once again stars Chief Inspector Armand Gamache of the Sûreté du Québec, Canada’s provincial police force. Gamache lives in the postcard-pretty outpost of Three Pines, which — Penny has always made clear — is based on the village in Canada’s Eastern Townships where she lives.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/books/review/30-BKS-LIST/30-BKS-LIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/30/books/review/30-BKS-LIST/30-BKS-LIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/books/review/30-BKS-LIST/30-BKS-LIST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/books/review/30-BKS-LIST/30-BKS-LIST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1050, 'width': 1050, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/books/review/30-BKS-LIST/30-BKS-LIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/30/books/review/30-BKS-LIST/30-BKS-LIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/books/review/30-BKS-LIST/30