'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/21/books/review/betty-ford-the-times-of-my-life.html', 'snippet': 'In which we consult the Book Review’s past to shed light on the books of the present. This week: Jane Howard on Betty Ford.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Isabel Wilkerson reviews Michelle Obama’s best-selling memoir, “Becoming.” Obama’s book joins a tradition of memoirs by former first ladies. In 1978, Jane Howard reviewed Betty Ford’s memoir, “The Times of My Life.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes From the Book Review Archives', 'kicker': 'From Our Archives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Our Archives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-12-21T15:27:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf484870-f6a8-5008-8ef6-6d51e7451ba7', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf484870-f6a8-5008-8ef6-6d51e7451ba7'}, {'abstract': 'Go big in preparing for the holiday: Make a tourtière for Christmas Eve. Or rest easy and make baked ziti.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/21/dining/what-to-cook-this-weekend-newsletter.html', 'snippet': 'Go big in preparing for the holiday: Make a tourtière for Christmas Eve. Or rest easy and make baked ziti.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. I wrote you last when I was en route to Miami for work, and it wasn’t until that evening when I was walking south on the beach, heading toward a sublime meal at 27, that I realized I neglected to give you a no-recipe recipe to cook on Wednesday, as is my usual custom. Apologies!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10marrrex-copy1