e Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d4f2354-0ea4-53d0-b3c1-6082a4f5786d', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d4f2354-0ea4-53d0-b3c1-6082a4f5786d'}, {'abstract': 'The celebrity chef’s latest cookbook, “Carla Hall’s Soul Food,” has plenty of recipes to ring in 2019.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/21/dining/carla-hall-soul-food-book.html', 'snippet': 'The celebrity chef’s latest cookbook, “Carla Hall’s Soul Food,” has plenty of recipes to ring in 2019.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carla Hall, the vivacious television celebrity and restaurateur, covers all bases in her latest book, showcasing Southern-inflected recipes pegged for “everyday” or “celebration” with plenty of overlap. For those seeking New Year’s inspiration, her book has plenty to offer, like black-eyed peas (considered lucky) in hummus, in a salad and in a vinaigrette sauce for pork. For dessert, as 2019 dawns, I’d head straight for the custardy nutmeg eggnog buttermilk pie or the gingerbread layer cake.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/26/dining/26burner4/26burner4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/26/dining/26burner4/26burner4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 688}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/26/dining/26burner4/26burner4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 893, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima