 None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f01c517-9b09-5993-9e5c-0f7bc3fc289b', 'word_count': 1337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f01c517-9b09-5993-9e5c-0f7bc3fc289b'}, {'abstract': 'In western Mongolia, hunting for fur and food with trained eagles is an important part of the local culture — and a way for tech-savvy teenagers to connect with their elders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/22/world/asia/mongolia-golden-eagle-festival.html', 'snippet': 'In western Mongolia, hunting for fur and food with trained eagles is an important part of the local culture — and a way for tech-savvy teenagers to connect with their elders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAYAN-OLGII, Mongolia — When school is done on Fridays, Zamanbol heads back home, finishes her homework and does her chores as typical teenagers do anywhere. On Saturdays, she saddles up her horse, treks deep into snow-capped mountains and hunts wild beasts with a trusted partner: her trained bird of prey.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/world/23mongolia-dispatch1/merlin_145517691_66cb8934-4d05-4c3d-80ff-10f8ce74cf28-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/23/world/23mongolia-dispatch1/merlin_145517691_66cb8934-4d05-4c3d-80ff-10f8ce74cf28-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/world/23mongolia-dispatch1/merlin_145517691_66cb8934-4d05-4c3d-80ff-10f8ce74cf28-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/23/world/23mongolia-dispatch1/merlin_145517691_66cb8934-4d0