'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-24T16:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Belcher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belcher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/241ecde1-cce3-5fa8-8241-1e2168134150', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/241ecde1-cce3-5fa8-8241-1e2168134150'}, {'abstract': 'Three hundred sixty-four days of the year, I am an independent person. Then I get to my mother’s house.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/24/opinion/christmas-adulthood-home.html', 'snippet': 'Three hundred sixty-four days of the year, I am an independent person. Then I get to my mother’s house.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I moved out of my parents’ house when I was 18. I headed off to college and with each passing year, grew older, became more self-reliant and hit new adult milestones, just as my parents had before me. Sure, some people might compare my mid-to-late 20s with my parents’ and say to me, “At your age, your parents had two children, a retirement fund and owned a house” and “You live in a walk-in closet,” but I think we all know the old saying: If you can’t touch every wall of your room while lying down, you’re spending too much on rent! Who needs a 401(k) when you have a Fitbit. Health is wealth. My Fitbit is still in the box but next year … next year is definitely the year I open it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/26/opinion/26limperisWeb/24limperisWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/26/opinion/26limperisWeb/24limperisWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/26/opinion/26limperisWeb/24limperisWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/26/opinion/26limperisWeb/24limperisWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/26/opinion/26limperisWeb/24limperisWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/26/opinion/26limperisWeb/24limperisWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/26/opinion/26limperisWeb/24limperisWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Adult Woman Goes Home for the Holidays', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greek-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-24T16:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alyssa Limperis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alyssa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Limperi