57-ade1b5af5539', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c186fd73-8d95-5746-b857-ade1b5af5539'}, {'abstract': 'Seen from space 50 years ago, Earth appeared as a gift to preserve and cherish. What happened?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/24/opinion/earth-space-christmas-eve-apollo-8.html', 'snippet': 'Seen from space 50 years ago, Earth appeared as a gift to preserve and cherish. What happened?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Christmas Eve 1968, human beings orbited the moon for the first time. News of the feat of NASA’s Apollo 8 mission dominated the front page of The New York Times the next day. Tucked away below the fold was an essay by the poet Archibald MacLeish, a reflection inspired by what he’d seen and heard the night before.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/17/science/24boulton-heithaus/24boulton-heithaus-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/17/science/24boulton-heithaus/24boulton-heithaus-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/17/science/24boulton-heithaus/24boulton-heithaus-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/17/science/24boulton-heithaus/24boulton-heithaus-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2008, 'width': 2008, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/17/science/24boulton-heithaus/24boulton-heithaus-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/17/science/24boulton-heithaus/24boulton-heithaus-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/17/science/24boulton-heithaus/24boulton-heithaus-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'We Are All Riders on the Same Planet ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We Are All Riders on This Planet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apollo Project', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-24T23:16:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Myer Boulton and Joseph Heithaus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'Myer', 'lastname': 'Boulton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heithaus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e1fd6a7-2e1e-5165-beee-554332bbc72b', 'word_count': 1230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e1fd6a7-2e1e-5165-beee-554332bbc72b'}, {'abstract': 'Patrick M. Shanahan, the White House pick for acting defense secretary, used his experience at Boeing to navigate, and battle, the Pentagon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/24/us/politics/patrick-shanahan-defense-secretary.html', 'snippet': 'Patrick M. Shanahan, the White House pick for acting defense secretary, used his experience at Boeing to navigate, and battle, the Pentagon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — When it was first announced last spring, President Trump’s proposal for a new Space Force was resisted by the Pentagon and ridiculed by late-night comics who envisioned Luke Skywalker in the military. But it found a champion in Patrick M. Shanahan, the deputy secretary of defense who will soon become the Pentagon’s acting chief.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/25/us/politics/25dc-military-print/merlin_148448808_a52f5559-6c60-48bf-8cc5-d4b4f7885518-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/25/us/politics/25dc-military-print/merlin_148448808_a52f5559-6c60-48bf-8cc5-d4b4f7885518-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/25/us/politics/25dc-military-print/merlin_148448808_a52f5559-6c60-48bf-8cc5-d4b4f7885518-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/25/us/politics/25dc-military-print/merlin_148448808_a52f5559-6c60-48bf-8cc5-d4b4f7885518-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/25/us/politics/25dc-military-print/25dc-military-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/25/us/politics/25dc-military-print/25dc-military-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/25/us/politics/25dc-military-print/25dc-military-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Not a ‘Department of No,’ New Defense Chief Turns Trump’s Demands Into Policy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Defense Secretary Supported Space Force And Will Back Trump', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shanahan, Patrick M (1962- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-24T23:22:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julian E. Barnes and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julian', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abefe8db-125f-56c0-8321-5f1a321ecc0f', 'word_count': 1228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abefe8db-125f-56c0-8321-5f1a321ecc0f'}, {'abstract': 'For millenniums, humans have tried to imagine the world in space. Fifty years ago, we finally saw it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/24/opinion/plato-earth-christmas-eve-apollo-8.html', 'snippet': 'For millenniums, humans have tried to imagine the world in space. Fifty years ago, we finally saw it.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Hey, don’t take that, it’s not scheduled,” Frank Borman said, joking to his fellow Apollo 8 astronauts, Bill Anders and James Lovell, on Dec. 24, 1968. They were orbiting the moon, farther from Earth than any humans had ever been. On the fourth pass, they were confronted by an extraordinary sight that jolted them out of their regimented procedures. There, seen through a small window, was Earth itself, rising out of the void. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/24/opinion/24Widmer-slide-QVB7/24Widmer-slide-QVB7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 928, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/24/opinion/24Widmer-slide-QVB7/24Widmer-slide-QVB7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 928}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/24/opinion/24Widmer-slide-QVB7/24Widmer-slide-QVB7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 662, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/24/opinion/24Widmer-slide-QVB7/24Widmer-slide-QVB7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1171, 'width': 757, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/24/opinion/24Widmer-slide-QVB7/24Widmer-slide-QVB7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/24/opinion/24Widmer-slide-QVB7/24Widmer-slide-QVB7-thumbStandard.jpg'