itish-Jamaican heritage and explore black male identity. As the designer says, her line “is about creating something for the guy who sits somewhere in between on the spectrum of masculinity and femininity.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/19/t-magazine/19tmag-asai-slide-8N4V/19tmag-asai-slide-8N4V-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/19/t-magazine/19tmag-asai-slide-8N4V/19tmag-asai-slide-8N4V-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/19/t-magazine/19tmag-asai-slide-8N4V/19tmag-asai-slide-8N4V-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/19/t-magazine/19tmag-asai-slide-8N4V/19tmag-asai-slide-8N4V-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/19/t-magazine/19tmag-asai-slide-8N4V/19tmag-asai-slide-8N4V-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/19/t-magazine/19tmag-asai-slide-8N4V/19tmag-asai-slide-8N4V-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/19/t-magazine/19tmag-asai-slide-8N4V/19tmag-asai-slide-8N4V-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '9 Brands We Discovered (and Loved) in 2018', 'kicker': 'T’s Best of 2018', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Two Thousand Eighteen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "D'heygere, Stephanie", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-26T14:25:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fe6c99e-1c18-574d-b235-8f187608c85a', 'word_count': 1106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fe6c99e-1c18-574d-b235-8f187608c85a'}, {'abstract': 'Music is competing for attention, and songs are just one of many products artists are hawking today: Aspiring pop stars need a new skill set, building careers that work like reality TV.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/26/arts/music/pop-music-social-media-distraction.html', 'snippet': 'Music is competing for attention, and songs are just one of many products artists are hawking today: Aspiring pop stars need a new skill set, building careers that work like reality TV.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the most widely praised releases of 2018 was “Whack World” by the singer and rapper Tierra Whack: 15 sly, smart songs, all accompanied by video clips, that each lasted only a minute. They went breezing by, lightheartedly addressing large ideas while alluding to decades of R&B and hip-hop. Her music was often skeletal — a handful of looped instruments — but most of the songs sounded complete, not truncated.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/arts/30yearend-pop2/merlin_147857643_8e0c5c65-4549-4946-b51d-49425b9dcf24-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/30/arts/30yearend-pop2/merlin_147857643_8e0c5c65-4549-4946-b51d-49425b9dcf24-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/arts/30yearend-pop2/merlin_147857643_8e0c5c65-4549-4946-b51d-49425b9dcf24-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/arts/30yearend-pop2/merlin_147857643_8e0c5c65-4549-4946-b51d-49425b9dcf24-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/arts/30yearend-pop2/30yearend-pop2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/30/arts/30yearend-pop2/30yearend-pop2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/arts/30yearend-pop2/30yearend-pop2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pop in the Era of Distraction', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Era of Distraction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}