arly 2000s hits like the Dior saddle bag and low-rise jeans suggests a perhaps fatal shortening of the cycle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Resale sites have come a long way since the dawn of eBay. Formerly app-based, the ever-rising secondhand site Depop recently added web checkout, functioning as a cross between Instagram and a sales platform. Its 10 million plus users have handles and followers. There are hashtags, you can “like” items and there’s a much stronger focus on styling and aesthetic. The coolest photo of the day will land you on the home page, and bam, you’re Depop-famous.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/27/fashion/2790SVINTAGE-2/merlin_148481442_4ad7f8ab-2889-4cbb-a74a-cf1a14868052-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 855, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/27/fashion/2790SVINTAGE-2/merlin_148481442_4ad7f8ab-2889-4cbb-a74a-cf1a14868052-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 855}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/27/fashion/2790SVINTAGE-2/merlin_148481442_4ad7f8ab-2889-4cbb-a74a-cf1a14868052-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 719, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/27/fashion/2790SVINTAGE-2/merlin_148481442_4ad7f8ab-2889-4cbb-a74a-cf1a14868052-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1438, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/27/fashion/2790SVINTAGE-2/27VINTAGE-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/27/fashion/2790SVINTAGE-2/27VINTAGE-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/27/fashion/2790SVINTAGE-2/27VINTAGE-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is ‘Vintage’ Clothing Over?', 'kicker': 'noted', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vintage Clothing Is Still Hot, but Trends Are Cycling Faster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thrift Shops', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-26T20:03:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rhiannon Picton-James', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rhiannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Picton-James', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e19fe5fa-dc10-5073-a3a6-8e902be30c0b', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e19fe5fa-dc10-5073-a3a6-8e902be30c0b'}, {'abstract': 'The best photos of 2018 that captured fame, fortune, fashion, fantasy and garbage fires.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/26/style/fabulous-pictures-of-famous-people.html', 'snippet': 'The best photos of 2018 that captured fame, fortune, fashion, fantasy and garbage fires.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the most satisfying memes of the last few years celebrates macaroni and cheese. Someone on social media will write “I made him mac and cheese …” or some such and share a revolting photo of a gelatinous dish of gray noodle slop. Then everyone will freak out and pile on. Sometimes the post is a joke, sometimes it’s real, and also sometimes it’s wings or meatloaf. In the case of Keisha Lance Bottoms, who also happens to be the mayor of Atlanta, it was just a sincere picture showing off her Christmas mac and cheese, to the extreme scorn and horror of the internet. Sure it did look a little dry, but who among us, you know? ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/fashion/30-BEST-PHOTOS-2018-met-kim/30-BEST-PHOTOS-2018-met-kim-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/30/fashion/30-BEST-PHOTOS-2018-met-kim/30-BEST-PHOTOS-2018-met-kim-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/fashion/30-BEST-PHOTOS-2018-met-kim/30-BEST-PHOTOS-2018-met-kim-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/fashion/30-BEST-PHOTOS-2018-met-kim/30-BEST-PHOTOS-2018-met-kim-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/fashion/30-BEST-PHOTOS-2018-met-kim/30-BEST-PHOTOS-2018-met-kim-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/30/fashion/30-BEST-PHOTOS-2018-met-kim/30-BEST-PHOTOS-2018-met-kim-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'sub