': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/463c7f0a-29ec-5b6c-b078-99efc671b6e0', 'word_count': 932, 'uri': 'nyt://article/463c7f0a-29ec-5b6c-b078-99efc671b6e0'}, {'abstract': 'The trip so nice we’re doing it twice. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/27/travel/meet-the-applicants-for-2019s-52-places-to-go-traveler.html', 'snippet': 'The trip so nice we’re doing it twice. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the second year in a row, we’re sending one lucky traveler to all 52 destinations on our annual Places to Go list. (Jada Yuan, our first Traveler, just finished her 52nd and final stop.) We got hundreds of applications from people around the world, with an impressive variety of backgrounds. We’ve picked our traveler — look out for the announcement soon — but in the meantime, we thought you might want to meet some of our favorite candidates. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meet the Applicants for 2019’s 52 Places to Go Traveler', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-27T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Video', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f9ac8a1-63f4-5327-9465-a503b2804d8c', 'word_count': 79, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f9ac8a1-63f4-5327-9465-a503b2804d8c'}, {'abstract': 'These brands want you to settle in and listen to the band. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/27/travel/5-hotels-booking-live-music-events.html', 'snippet': 'These brands want you to settle in and listen to the band. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Turning their lobbies, pools, bars and rooftops into concert venues lets hotels bring music-scene energy on-site. Some are following the example of festivals like Coachella by hosting days-long events, while other are throwing one-time intimate concerts. Here, some of the hotels that have music events planned in 2019. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/travel/30music-sidebar1/merlin_144181401_1c6e54e4-3150-4b2e-9393-3ac68451e499-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/30/travel/30music-sidebar1/merlin_144181401_1c6e54e4-3150-4b2e-9393-3ac68451e499-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/travel/30music-sidebar1/merlin_144181401_1c6e54e4-3150-4b2e-9393-3ac68451e499-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/travel/30music-sidebar1/merlin_144181401_1c6e54e4-3150-4b2e-9393-3ac68451e499-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/travel/30music-sidebar1/30music-sidebar1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/30/travel/30music-sidebar1/30music-sidebar1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/travel/30music-sidebar1/30music-sidebar1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 15