, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60106ee4-fd64-587a-82e7-4db9fd12b98a', 'word_count': 1531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60106ee4-fd64-587a-82e7-4db9fd12b98a'}, {'abstract': 'At the Frick, an exhibition devoted to Luigi Valadier, the Roman silversmith to popes, sovereigns and aristocrats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/27/arts/design/decorative-arts-frick-collection-valadier.html', 'snippet': 'At the Frick, an exhibition devoted to Luigi Valadier, the Roman silversmith to popes, sovereigns and aristocrats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Money can’t buy you everything, but in 18th-century Rome, it could underwrite some pretty amazing acquisitions: a shoebox-size, neo-Classical, gilt silver casket for your wine; a Rococo clock consisting almost entirely of vivacious curves (not a straight line anywhere); or an exquisite bronze miniature of a famous Greek sculpture like the Apollo Belvedere, just the thing for a royal study.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/28/arts/28valadier-oak-01/merlin_146839101_d13b650a-9d2f-4510-9ed1-337ae0810b7f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/28/arts/28valadier-oak-01/merlin_146839101_d13b650a-9d2f-4510-9ed1-337ae0810b7f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/28/arts/28valadier-oak-01/merlin_146839101_d13b650a-9d2f-4510-9ed1-337ae0810b7f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/28/arts/