hasta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Darlington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a58eabdf-95db-5739-8477-6f939533b1c1', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a58eabdf-95db-5739-8477-6f939533b1c1'}, {'abstract': 'Fred Piscop sends 2018 out with a bifurcated Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/29/crosswords/variety-split-decisions.html', 'snippet': 'Fred Piscop sends 2018 out with a bifurcated Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VARIETY PUZZLE — We gravitate toward the second Sunday puzzle for a challenge that breaks the standard crossword mold; sometimes the differences aren’t readily apparent, but Split Decisions is one that’s completely off the grid, if you will.  For me, that difference leads to uncertainty, which usually leads to extra care and time in my approach, since I tend to be a little afraid of change.  But at least we’re here, right?  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Split Decisions', 'kicker': 'SUNDAY VARIETY COLUMN', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-29T16:40:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59b8aa22-57f4-5a1b-a27c-ed18bbb4fc81', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59b8aa22-57f4-5a1b-a27c-ed18bbb4fc81'}, {'abstract': 'Competitors were supposed to have their shot at Olympic glory in 2022. Now 2026 looks more likely as the sport tries to reach a critical mass of quality. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/29/sports/nordic-combined-olympics.html', 'snippet': 'Competitors were supposed to have their shot at Olympic glory in 2022. Now 2026 looks more likely as the sport tries to reach a critical mass of quality. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'STEAMBOAT SPRINGS, Colo. — Tara Geraghty-Moats was 11 the first time she took a big trip for a ski competition. Her mother insisted she was still too young to travel with a team, so the pair set off from Vermont, boarded a plane and flew to Steamboat Springs for the 2005 ski jumping and Nordic combined Junior Olympics.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/27/sports/27nordic-01/merlin_148374822_b339e25d-b130-4208-992f-152f5a84e1b1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/27/sports/27nordic-01/merlin_148374822_b339e25d-b130-4208-992f-152f5a84e1b1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/27/sports/27nordic-01/merlin_148374822_b339e25d-b130-4208-992f-152f5a84e1b1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/27/sports/27nordic-01/merlin_148374822_b339e25d-b130-4208-992f-152f5a84e1b1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1389, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/27/sports/27nordic-01/27nordic-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy':