d': 'nyt://article/7a3f02a3-6a38-5ac4-8a97-b672fef39868', 'word_count': 1346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a3f02a3-6a38-5ac4-8a97-b672fef39868'}, {'abstract': 'A reluctant evolution is taking place in residential drug treatment for opioid addiction. Here’s a look at one center’s wary shift.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/29/health/opioid-rehab-abstinence-medication.html', 'snippet': 'A reluctant evolution is taking place in residential drug treatment for opioid addiction. Here’s a look at one center’s wary shift.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MURFREESBORO, Tenn. — Just past a cemetery along a country road, an addiction treatment center called JourneyPure at the River draws hundreds of patients a month who are addicted to opioids and other drugs. They divide their days between therapy sessions, songwriting, communing with horses and climbing through a treetop ropes course. After dinner, they’re driven into town in white vans for 12-step meetings.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/science/30OPIOID-TENNESSEE-topper2/merlin_148373247_94fdfd7d-db14-4cfd-9473-62a8a409b843-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/30/science/30OPIOID-TENNESSEE-topper2/merlin_148373247_94fdfd7d-db14-4cfd-9473-62a8a409b843-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/science/30OPIOID-TENNESSEE-topper2/merlin_148373247_94fdfd7d-db14-4cfd-9473-62a8a409b843-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/30/science/30OPIOID-TENNESSEE-topper2/merlin_148373247_94