o Provide Doping Data', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia Fails to Provide Doping Data and Faces the Risk of New Penalties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2018)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Anti-Doping Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-31T20:36:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tariq Panja', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tariq', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Panja', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b788e96-907b-5eab-b3e4-d95281f6e25f', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b788e96-907b-5eab-b3e4-d95281f6e25f'}, {'abstract': 'Alison Roman wants you to spend less time in the kitchen and more time at the table. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/31/dining/how-to-eat-in-2019.html', 'snippet': 'Alison Roman wants you to spend less time in the kitchen and more time at the table. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'I had always maintained that I’d be the kind of person who makes time for cooking, regardless of how busy I became. It is, after all, my job, my hobby, my creative outlet and how I connect with people.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/02/dining/02ROMAN-Cover/merlin_148228464_162ab490-5379-4696-91b0-436863f0f2d7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/01/02/dining/02ROMAN-Cover/merlin_148228464_162ab490-5379-4696-91b0-436863f0f2d7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/02/dining/02ROMAN-Cover/merlin_148228464_162ab490-5379-4696-91b0-436863f0f2d7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/02/dining/02ROMAN-Cover/merlin_148228464_162ab490-5379-4696-91b0-436863f0f2d7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/02/dining/02ROMAN-Cover/merlin_148228464_162ab490-5379-4696-91b0-436863f0f2d7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/01/02/dining/02ROMAN-Cover/merlin_148228464_162ab490-5379-4696-91b0-436863f0f2d7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/02/dining/02ROMAN-Cover/merlin_148228464_162ab490-5379-4696-91b0-436863f0f2d7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Eat in 2019', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How To Eat This Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poultry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Noodles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salmon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-31T20:48:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Roman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb5a226d-dcf3-58f0-b2ea-496d0df66551', 'word_count': 984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb5a226d-dcf3-58f0-b2ea-496d0df66551'}, {'abstract': 'There is no commercial, cultural or scientific justification for killing these magnificent creatures. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/31/opinion/editorials/japan-whale-hunt-whaling.html', 'snippet': 'There is no commercial, cultural or scientific justification for killing these magnificent creatures. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Japan, in many respects a model global citizen, has long been an outlier on whaling, an industry that most nations have abandoned as cruel, unnecessary and a danger to the survival of the great mammals of the seas, but that the Japanese claim as part of their culture. That divide has come to a head with Japan’s exit from the International Whaling Commission, a politically motivated decision Tokyo should reconsider.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/31/opinion/31whaling-edt/merlin_148499787_2aa87000-7442-4c6a-bc03-db96d17d2e04-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/31/opinion/31whaling-edt/merlin_148499787_2aa87000-7442-4c6a-bc03-db96d17d2e04-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/31/opinion/31whaling-edt/merlin_148499787_2aa87000-7442-4c6a-bc03-db96d17d2e04-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 648, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/31/opinion/31whaling-edt/merlin_148499787_2aa87000-7442-4c6a-bc03-db96d17d2e04-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1297, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/31/opinion/31whaling-edt/31whaling-edt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/31/opinion/31whaling-edt/31whaling-edt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/31/opinion/31whaling-edt/31whaling-edt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan: Stop Slaughtering Whales', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whales and Whaling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Greenpeace', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Whaling Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sea Shepherd Conservation Society', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southern Ocean', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-12-31T20:53:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Editorials', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/00a689c5-648d-5076-8c88-e467ca44132d', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00a689c5-648d-5076-8c88-e467ca44132d'}, {'abstract': 'Andrea Chesman’s latest cookbook shows you how to use animal fats for cooking and baking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/31/dining/the-fat-kitchen-book.html', 'snippet': 'Andrea Chesman’s latest cookbook shows you how to use animal fats for cooking and baking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the dead of winter, “The Fat Kitchen” could not be more timely. It’s a guide to preparing and using animal fats, indulgently or sparingly, in all sorts of delectable ways. Not just any animal fats, though. The author, a food writer who lives in Vermont, insists on fats from pasture-raised creatures, preferably rendered at home. No industrial lard in her fridge. In a book as dense as a doctoral dissertation, she covers chemistry, health, commercialization, safety, traditions and cooking. She deals with butter only briefly because it’s so familiar. Tempting recipes include onion confit, rich chicken paprikash and roasted cabbage. Cakes and especially pastries made with lard and duck fat may open new horizons.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/02/dining/02BurnerBook1/merlin_148531617_48049db4-1b50-45c1-a76f-ca0f97eb8693-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/01/02/dining/02BurnerBook1/merlin_148531617_48049db4-1b50-45c1-a76f-ca0f97eb8693-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 735}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/02/dining/02BurnerBo