d_paragraph': 'In 2016, filmmaker Samantha Knowles set out to document the controversy that erupted in Warwick, the small town she grew up in outside New York City, when a blue line was painted in support of police on a street in the town center. After the film premiered in The Times this year, conversations began anew about what has changed in Warwick, and what has remained the same. We caught up with town residents and the filmmaker for their thoughts on what lessons we can take from a divided community trying to find common ground. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/08/20/opinion/00-Warwick-01/merlin_141970215_87c3f622-5d5a-4e39-8e0f-5a2c7c19ad59-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 486, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/08/20/opinion/00-Warwick-01/merlin_141970215_87c3f622-5d5a-4e39-8e0f-5a2c7c19ad59-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 486}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/08/20/opinion/00-Warwick-01/merlin_141970215_87c3f622-5d5a-4e39-8e0f-5a2c7c19ad59-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 829, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/08/20/opinion/00-Warwick-01/merlin_141970215_87c3f622-5d5a-4e39-8e0f-5a2c7c19ad59-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1659, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/08/20/opinion/00-Warwick-01/00-Warwick-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/08/20/opinion/00-Warwick-01/00-Warwick-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwid